1
00:02:07,245 --> 00:02:16,635
Visit turkision.com for more!

2
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:19,239
Osman Bey is coming!

3
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:23,039
Osman Bey is coming

4
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:33,239
Osman Bey is coming!
Osman Bey is bringing the prisoners!

5
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:45,039
Welcome Osman Bey! Long live Osman Bey!

6
00:02:45,240 --> 00:03:20,599
Welcome Osman Bey! Long live OsmarTBey!

7
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:35,239
May witches take your life!

8
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:41,799
May souls fall onto you like nightmares, Osman!

9
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:49,159
Welcome Osman Bey!

10
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:50,679
Peace be with you.

11
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:53,199
Peace be upon you.

12
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:59,359
Welcome, my Bey.

13
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:08,559
Come on then.

14
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:34,759
No.

15
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:39,279
Don't make the Beys kneel.

16
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:51,679
Oh people, my Beys, my Alps.

17
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:55,079
Mekece Castle...

18
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:58,399
...with the help of Allah...

19
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:00,999
...has become Kayi's property.

20
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:04,879
Thank Allah.

21
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:11,359
Long live Osman Bey!

22
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:14,399
Thank you, thank you.

23
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:19,559
Thank you.

24
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:25,119
Thank Allah, without any martyrs...

25
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:30,199
...we made them kneel and bow before us.

26
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:43,919
And no one stopped us from our conquest.

27
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:52,159
We got rid of the soldiers in Mekece castle.

28
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:57,719
And we stopped their evil alliance!

29
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:10,839
If Allah permits, Mekece will be our
vanguard for the upcoming conquests.

30
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:16,119
If Allah permits.

31
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:25,399
Come on now,
share the loot among alps and people.

32
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:29,479
Long live Osman Bey!

33
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:37,239
Thank you, thank you, thank you.
Long live to you as well.

34
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,839
And the prisoners...

35
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:48,479
...will wait to hear their verdict.

36
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:56,719
They will wait.

37
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:04,799
What's this disgrace!? Who do you
think you are to imprison my Bey!?

38
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:08,399
We are the owners
of the lands you step on, Melike Hatun!

39
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:11,719
Know your place.

40
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:30,959
Osman brought Lords and Beys along with him.

41
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,959
He has the control.

42
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:37,839
We have to run. We must escape. Come on.

43
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:41,759
We'll escape. We'll escape.

44
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:46,559
Before vultures eat my soldiers flesh away...

45
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:49,719
...we'll destroy this tribe.

46
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,079
Beys are here.

47
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:04,799
Now you'll talk.

48
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:10,079
Alps. That's enough rest. Untie them.

49
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,719
We're good.

50
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,239
Don't bother.

51
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:19,599
The sun warms my bones.

52
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:20,919
Yes.

53
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:22,919
It's outdoors.

54
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:24,919
The tent will suffocate me.

55
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:26,919
It's outdoors?

56
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,919
The tent will suffocate you?

57
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:34,639
Konur.

58
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:44,319
We'll see...

59
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:47,919
...if you can be this happy...

60
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:50,599
...when your skin is pulled away.

61
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:53,759
Alps. Untie them.

62
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:09,679
Walk.

63
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:10,959
Walk.

64
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:13,799
Congratulations my Bey.

65
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:17,559
Your decision will herald..

66
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:19,559
..even bigger wars.

67
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:23,519
I could kill them all.

68
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:27,879
But our Ghaza goal won't
lose a single drop of blood.

69
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:31,559
But...

70
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:34,639
...Ulcay keeps interrupting us.

71
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:37,439
Now...

72
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:40,759
..if we don't reveal he's a traitor...

73
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:43,039
...we'll be guilty.

74
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:49,119
Did Boran and Konur make him talk?

75
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:52,239
Rukneddin The Judge's burial site...

76
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:55,759
We thought only the murderer,
Orhan and Elcim knew about it.

77
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:58,999
But Ulcay knows it.

78
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:02,439
He killed Rukneddin The Judge my Bey.

79
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,479
We know it.

80
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,679
Then he killed Ahmet too.

81
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:12,959
We must reveal it.

82
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:16,479
The dog won't talk even if we torture him.

83
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,719
We'll let them get away.

84
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:25,439
Well...

85
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:29,559
That's why
I made Boran and Konur go with him.

86
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:32,399
They can earn his trust.

87
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:35,559
We'll go after him when the time comes.

88
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:39,719
We'll only know the truth when the dog is free.

89
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:43,399
Then we'll release the dog.

90
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:45,559
Exactly.

91
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,599
We will.

92
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:57,999
What did
they give you to betray Osman Bey?

93
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:02,599
Release me and I'll tell you.

94
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:07,759
You said...

95
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:11,439
...you'd always side with us Boran Bey.

96
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:13,559
What happened?

97
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:15,559
I helped them wake up.

98
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:19,519
They saw who Osman Bey really is.

99
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:20,799
You...

100
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:27,439
You dog, Ulcay.

101
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:32,119
You helped them wake up?

102
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:35,399
Now I'll gauge out your eyes.

103
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:38,719
We'll see if you can still talk.

104
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:43,839
Baysungur.

105
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:15,919
A dog will only shut up with a good beating.

106
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:19,879
We have to kill Osman now.

107
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:21,879
If not he'll kill us if he finds us.

108
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:24,119
We're going to kill him...

109
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:26,719
Once we're out of here...

110
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:30,679
...I'm going to
burn him to death alongside his tribe.

111
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:05,519
With so many lies...

112
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:08,359
...you tried to truck us.

113
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,719
But...

114
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:19,559
...just as you always do against the truth...

115
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:22,159
...you lost once again.

116
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:33,199
Infidel.

117
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:36,519
To find a way to defeat us...

118
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:39,079
...they always make a move.

119
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:43,239
What about you?

120
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,199
The beys of Turks.

121
00:13:56,840 --> 00:14:00,119
How did you become a part of this?

122
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:02,159
What did you gain?

123
00:14:02,160 --> 00:14:04,759
Tell me, what?

124
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:10,319
You lost your land.

125
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:13,079
You have a stain in your past now.

126
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:27,439
You can't keep us here.

127
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:30,479
Byzantine will make you
pay for it Osman Bey.

128
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:35,639
Ask your own beys whatever you want.

129
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:39,239
But we Byzantine...

130
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,439
We of course have conditions..

131
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:52,279
...to forsake your life.

132
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:55,639
Tell the Emperor.

133
00:14:55,640 --> 00:15:00,759
You're going to let go of the Turks
you're holding captive in Byzantine lands.

134
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:03,839
Those who you arrested for nothing...

135
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:07,159
...those you're keeping for a ransom. All of them.

136
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:16,279
Only then...

137
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:20,039
...will you make it out of here alive.

138
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:22,559
If riot...

139
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:26,359
...only your dead bodies will leave these lands.

140
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:35,319
Don't forget these.

141
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:37,239
Wait here.

142
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:52,119
Come on, this way.

143
00:16:04,440 --> 00:16:06,679
Let's leave before the alps wake up.

144
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:09,639
Where is the stable?

145
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:11,599
It's not possible to go there.

146
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:12,759
It's too close to the middle.

147
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:15,719
Am I to be scared of a handful of alps?

148
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:17,559
I'll open up my path with blood.

149
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:18,959
Ulcay.

150
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:21,039
Put your sword away.

151
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:23,879
We'll leave without making a noise.

152
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:28,199
Come on.

153
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:45,799
Against my beys...

154
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:49,359
...I have a code that holds me back.

155
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:51,839
But...

156
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:55,799
...my religion tells me to be...

157
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:59,279
...strict towards your kind.

158
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:04,999
I'm declaring war on Byzantine now.

159
00:17:05,079 --> 00:17:06,719
We won't stop until...

160
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:10,199
...your land is our land.

161
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:19,759
Take them away now.

162
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:32,839
Come on, Beys.

163
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:54,519
By working with the infidels...

164
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:57,839
...you made a mistake.

165
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:04,039
When we wanted to ride our
horses in those lands for ghaza...

166
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:09,959
...you stopped us from ghaza.

167
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:16,639
From now on, no one will hide behind trade.

168
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:24,359
We will not allow speaking of
prosperity, and poisoning the Beys!

169
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:29,359
And no Turk tribe will..

170
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:34,519
...trade in Byzantine lands!

171
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:38,279
What are you talking about Osman Bey?

172
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:42,439
How dare you to interfere in our trade?

173
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:48,239
We exposed you.

174
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:53,119
But I haven't told you
about your verdict yet.

175
00:18:55,360 --> 00:19:00,639
You should pray, so that I won't hang you.

176
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:37,639
Ulcay got the bait.

177
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:38,999
He did!

178
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:43,319
Konur Bey hit me really hard to make him believe.

179
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:45,399
It would be tough for me if he hadn't believed.

180
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:49,119
Well, you deserved it
after saying all those words.

181
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:53,519
Well, Boran Bey acted mercifully.

182
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:58,039
So, what will happen now?

183
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:02,959
Konur and Boran will bring the truth to Osman Bey.

184
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:12,519
As long as there are Beys like you...

185
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:16,199
...we don't need any enemies!

186
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:23,079
Your pride and ambition did this to you

187
00:20:23,520 --> 00:20:27,079
For what? Just for power...

188
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:31,479
...and might! Tell me, what did it get you?

189
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,759
What do you have now? Beys!

190
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:41,359
I will tell you.

191
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:44,479
In these lands...

192
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:48,959
...you have no authority!

193
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:57,799
In these frontiers, from now on,
only we will be the ones to do trade.

194
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:02,279
Everything will be under our control.

195
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:13,599
Bursa, Iznik, Constantinople...

196
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:18,119
...from East to West, and West to East...

197
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:22,759
...I stopped all the trade!

198
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:28,159
No one...

199
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:31,799
...will trade.

200
00:21:32,880 --> 00:21:39,439
You are killing our livelihood, Osman Bey!

201
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:45,039
How are you going to stop our trade?

202
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:49,319
Yakup Bey, you seem to not understand.

203
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:53,279
Every caravan that comes out of your lands...

204
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:57,439
...will be attacked.

205
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:10,639
Then, you are...

206
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:13,679
...waging
war upon us, together with Byzantine.

207
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:20,199
All the things you said are
reasons for war, Osman Bey!

208
00:22:20,640 --> 00:22:23,439
Wait, Yakup Bey.

209
00:22:23,440 --> 00:22:28,039
I am not finished yet.
There are things you haven't heard.

210
00:22:29,040 --> 00:22:30,279
Well...

211
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:32,279
You're so proud of...

212
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:34,479
...the frontier market.

213
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:39,479
From now on..

214
00:22:41,600 --> 00:22:42,959
...it is Kayi property.

215
00:22:59,360 --> 00:23:02,359
GERMIYANOGLU BORDER - FRONTIER MARKET

216
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:07,199
The Frontier Market
is Kayi property from now on.

217
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:13,519
Come on. Don't wait!

218
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:16,359
Hang Kayi's sacred flag.

219
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:17,439
Do it!

220
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:35,319
Allah is the Greatest!

221
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:41,159
This flag will shine like a star...

222
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:44,599
...between all the Turkmens...

223
00:23:44,760 --> 00:23:46,799
...and welcome everyone, I hope.

224
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:48,799
I hope so, Aykurt.

225
00:23:49,240 --> 00:23:50,799
I hope so.

226
00:23:56,280 --> 00:23:58,279
What are you talking about, Osman Bey?

227
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:00,639
I have never heard such a thing.

228
00:24:01,240 --> 00:24:05,399
As long as you act scared...

229
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:12,159
...you'll see many things you've never seen.

230
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:14,759
Osman Bey...

231
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:17,279
You know that...

232
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:21,479
...what you did will have repercussions.

233
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:28,679
You should be happy...

234
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:32,159
...that in return for what you did...

235
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:35,839
...I only take your castle and market.

236
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:45,839
Come on.

237
00:24:47,040 --> 00:24:49,079
Take the Beys to their tent.

238
00:24:50,960 --> 00:24:52,839
Until I release my judgment...

239
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:55,679
...they'll be treated as captives.

240
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:59,359
Go on.

241
00:25:20,720 --> 00:25:23,679
Turk's great Beys...

242
00:25:23,680 --> 00:25:25,679
Look what you did.

243
00:25:29,040 --> 00:25:32,479
My Bey. Someone came a long way to see you.

244
00:25:35,320 --> 00:25:37,079
Peace be with you Osman Bey.

245
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:40,519
The far away Turk lands send you regards.

246
00:25:40,520 --> 00:25:42,519
Peace be upon you.

247
00:25:42,840 --> 00:25:44,399
We send our regards too.

248
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:46,999
You came from a long way.

249
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:50,359
Tell me. What do you wish to say?

250
00:25:50,360 --> 00:25:53,359
We heard you aim for Ghaza.
We wish to fight with you.

251
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:58,079
Everyone wants to do the same.

252
00:25:58,200 --> 00:26:00,719
You will side with me in war.

253
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:04,519
Show us the way and we'll fight in front of you.

254
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:07,839
When the time comes, we'll
die for Ghaza, Osman Bey.

255
00:26:07,840 --> 00:26:09,839
Praise be.

256
00:26:10,400 --> 00:26:12,839
People come and people go.

257
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:14,559
Thank you.

258
00:26:15,120 --> 00:26:16,679
Welcome to our land.

259
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:18,679
Thank you my Bey.

260
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:22,119
Come on.

261
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:28,079
Today we'll have victory.

262
00:26:28,240 --> 00:26:29,439
Come on.

263
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:44,599
Who are you?

264
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:46,919
Stand back.

265
00:27:03,520 --> 00:27:06,359
I'm here to
take you to Constantine Paleologos.

266
00:27:07,880 --> 00:27:09,799
Greetings to my friend.

267
00:27:10,640 --> 00:27:12,079
Put down your swords.

268
00:27:14,480 --> 00:27:15,639
Who's Constantine?

269
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:17,759
What does he want?

270
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:19,759
Let's go. No time.

271
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:40,239
I'll be back for Osman.

272
00:27:40,240 --> 00:27:41,959
Go to the Green Valley.

273
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:43,479
I'll find you there.

274
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:46,359
Then, I'll tell you everything.

275
00:27:59,520 --> 00:28:02,319
They're running away just like that.

276
00:28:02,520 --> 00:28:04,399
Who are they Konur?

277
00:28:04,440 --> 00:28:06,079
Where are they going?

278
00:28:06,080 --> 00:28:09,839
Brother, we have to follow them.
They will do something, it's clear as day.

279
00:28:09,840 --> 00:28:12,479
How can we keep up with them with running, Boran?

280
00:28:13,960 --> 00:28:16,519
Besides, if we go they will know.

281
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:20,439
That jackal will come back to his inn.

282
00:28:20,480 --> 00:28:22,679
Everything will be revealed soon.

283
00:28:23,520 --> 00:28:25,839
His days are numbered now.

284
00:28:33,480 --> 00:28:34,919
Alps.

285
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:37,759
Prepare the horses, come on.

286
00:28:37,760 --> 00:28:40,799
We have lots to do.

287
00:28:43,440 --> 00:28:45,279
Gunduz Bey.

288
00:28:54,440 --> 00:28:56,479
Do you have time?

289
00:28:56,480 --> 00:28:58,959
You heard Osman Bey.

290
00:28:58,960 --> 00:29:03,119
We have to stop the
Byzantine help Bursa is getting.

291
00:29:03,520 --> 00:29:07,119
I'm going to Sakarya to build some tribes.

292
00:29:07,120 --> 00:29:11,519
If what you're going
to say isn't something very important...

293
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:13,719
...then let's speak later.

294
00:29:14,320 --> 00:29:16,399
Gunduz Bey.

295
00:29:20,120 --> 00:29:22,199
The thing that happened the other day.

296
00:29:22,200 --> 00:29:24,439
Those weren't pleasant.

297
00:29:26,720 --> 00:29:28,959
I'm sorry.

298
00:29:30,360 --> 00:29:33,039
I didn't mean to shout at you.

299
00:29:33,200 --> 00:29:36,959
I respect both your age and experience.

300
00:29:38,080 --> 00:29:39,399
Besides...

301
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:41,359
..we shouldn't be on bad terms.

302
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:44,119
We have so much to worry about...

303
00:29:44,120 --> 00:29:46,839
...so we should hold
each other close right Gunduz Bey?

304
00:29:48,200 --> 00:29:50,719
I've fought with the...

305
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:54,239
...Mongols a for years.

306
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:57,959
I've seen a lot of bloodshed and death.

307
00:29:58,560 --> 00:30:03,519
So a bey who is old enough to be my son...

308
00:30:03,520 --> 00:30:06,239
...shouting at me did bother me.

309
00:30:09,160 --> 00:30:10,679
But...

310
00:30:10,680 --> 00:30:14,119
...you did what
is suitable for you.

311
00:30:14,120 --> 00:30:16,439
And you destroyed that feeling.

312
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:21,639
I'm sorry too.

313
00:30:21,640 --> 00:30:23,999
I shouldn't have messed with your knowledge.

314
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:26,999
Not at all, Gunduz Bey.

315
00:30:28,920 --> 00:30:31,079
Let me tell you this.

316
00:30:31,080 --> 00:30:33,959
Let's
forget what happened Gunduz Bey.

317
00:30:35,080 --> 00:30:40,159
We're all going to be wrapped
in that white cloth one day.

318
00:30:41,440 --> 00:30:43,839
I give you my blessings.

319
00:30:43,840 --> 00:30:46,199
Please give me yours too.

320
00:30:46,200 --> 00:30:49,079
Of course Gunduz Bey, thank you.

321
00:30:49,520 --> 00:30:51,919
But why do you say that?

322
00:30:52,280 --> 00:30:55,959
We're going to fight along
side each other a lot more.

323
00:30:55,960 --> 00:30:58,479
Don't say that.

324
00:30:59,360 --> 00:31:01,679
A big war is on the horizon.

325
00:31:01,760 --> 00:31:06,399
Gaza asks the soldiers to bleed.

326
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:10,879
In this world where we
can't even control a breath...

327
00:31:10,880 --> 00:31:14,599
...we might live today and be gone tomorrow.

328
00:31:16,520 --> 00:31:21,359
How can one know when
they will give their last breath?

329
00:31:21,360 --> 00:31:23,239
Of course we can't.

330
00:31:23,240 --> 00:31:26,799
That's why until the day we
die we have to live freely...

331
00:31:26,800 --> 00:31:28,599
...and try to be happy right?

332
00:31:28,600 --> 00:31:31,479
Alright, Orhan Bey.

333
00:31:36,560 --> 00:31:38,839
Duty calls.

334
00:31:38,840 --> 00:31:41,639
I trust you with each other..

335
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:48,159
...and I trust you with my daughter Elcim.

336
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:52,439
Hold each other tight like the nail and the flesh.

337
00:31:52,720 --> 00:31:54,119
Don't forget.

338
00:31:54,400 --> 00:31:57,559
Elcim has no one but you.

339
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:01,359
Don't worry Gunduz Bey.

340
00:32:01,360 --> 00:32:03,359
I'll give my life away instead of...

341
00:32:03,360 --> 00:32:06,919
...letting Elcim get hurt.

342
00:32:09,280 --> 00:32:10,479
Come on.

343
00:32:10,480 --> 00:32:12,439
May Allah protect you.

344
00:32:12,440 --> 00:32:14,399
Thank you Gunduz Bey.

345
00:32:14,400 --> 00:32:16,399
With peace, Gunduz Bey.

346
00:32:16,400 --> 00:32:17,439
With peace.

347
00:32:19,160 --> 00:32:20,839
Come on.

348
00:32:22,920 --> 00:32:24,759
Let's hit the road.

349
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:27,479
We have a long road ahead of us.

350
00:32:42,320 --> 00:32:45,999
My brave brother. Come on.

351
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:48,199
Alright, brother.

352
00:32:53,400 --> 00:32:58,839
Holofira, the important matter
you wanted to talk about.

353
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:04,679
What's it?

354
00:33:05,800 --> 00:33:12,199
My duty is over, so
I want to leave the tribe, Osman Bey.

355
00:33:20,720 --> 00:33:23,679
You are like our daughter, Holofira.

356
00:33:23,680 --> 00:33:27,719
Even without a duty, you are always welcomed here.

357
00:33:27,960 --> 00:33:31,839
And, where will you go?

358
00:33:33,400 --> 00:33:36,159
Is this about...

359
00:33:37,320 --> 00:33:40,639
...Orhan and Elcim?

360
00:33:43,200 --> 00:33:49,839
As long as I am here, there will always
be a dark cloud over their marriage.

361
00:33:50,760 --> 00:33:53,879
I don't want to harm their marriage.

362
00:33:54,400 --> 00:33:59,519
Since the beginning, the best
option for all of us was for me to leave.

363
00:34:01,360 --> 00:34:03,759
Do you want to go to Constantinople?

364
00:34:03,760 --> 00:34:04,999
No.

365
00:34:05,560 --> 00:34:10,839
If you allow it,
I want to stay in a monastery in Bursa...

366
00:34:11,440 --> 00:34:16,478
...until you conquer it.
That's the heart of Byzantine.

367
00:34:17,040 --> 00:34:22,399
Even if I leave the tribe, I
want to continue helping you.

368
00:34:28,920 --> 00:34:32,478
They know that you have
been on our side for a while.

369
00:34:32,480 --> 00:34:35,599
They will hold a grudge against you.

370
00:34:36,120 --> 00:34:39,279
This will be a tough duty.

371
00:34:41,320 --> 00:34:44,119
My own aunt sent me to my death.

372
00:34:46,360 --> 00:34:50,239
So it's not hard for me to fight against them.

373
00:34:51,080 --> 00:34:58,159
I will convince them that you tricked
me and wanted to use me as a slave.

374
00:35:00,080 --> 00:35:04,719
Holofira, I know you are a brave girl.

375
00:35:05,080 --> 00:35:06,519
But...

376
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:11,759
...I can't put you in a danger like this.

377
00:35:13,600 --> 00:35:19,279
After all you did for me, I
owe it to Kayis, Osman Bey.

378
00:35:19,680 --> 00:35:23,319
When you conquer Bursa one day...

379
00:35:23,680 --> 00:35:27,759
...I will be happy to know that I did my part.

380
00:35:28,200 --> 00:35:30,919
Please allow me to do that.

381
00:35:35,160 --> 00:35:38,319
You are showing great courage for us.

382
00:35:40,400 --> 00:35:43,999
So we can't stand in your way.

383
00:35:44,880 --> 00:35:46,759
Okay, my girl.

384
00:35:47,480 --> 00:35:49,439
May Allah enlighten your path.

385
00:35:49,720 --> 00:35:52,079
Thank you.

386
00:36:20,760 --> 00:36:24,239
Ambush! To arms!

387
00:36:29,280 --> 00:36:31,439
Who are you?

388
00:36:56,160 --> 00:37:01,239
Whose tail did I step on this
time to be ambushed like this?

389
00:37:01,680 --> 00:37:04,199
What do you want? Who are you?

390
00:37:04,320 --> 00:37:08,199
Don't worry, you will get to know me!

391
00:37:09,640 --> 00:37:11,959
Take him!

392
00:37:31,680 --> 00:37:33,399
Did you think clearly Holofira?

393
00:37:33,920 --> 00:37:35,199
I did Gonca.

394
00:37:36,840 --> 00:37:37,479
I made up my mind.

395
00:37:38,680 --> 00:37:39,959
I'll live in the Monastery.

396
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:43,599
What will you do there all alone?

397
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:45,879
Can't you stay here?

398
00:37:46,040 --> 00:37:48,919
All good things come to
an end eventually, Fatma.

399
00:37:57,560 --> 00:37:59,839
The times we spent together...

400
00:37:59,880 --> 00:38:01,399
...were valuable.

401
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:25,119
You're leaving.

402
00:38:27,240 --> 00:38:28,319
I am.

403
00:38:38,840 --> 00:38:40,839
It's time to say goodbye.

404
00:38:43,160 --> 00:38:44,439
Goodbye...

405
00:38:44,880 --> 00:38:46,359
...Orhan Bey.

406
00:38:48,880 --> 00:38:49,999
Go safely.

407
00:38:52,600 --> 00:38:53,679
Lord's daughter.

408
00:39:02,880 --> 00:39:04,479
I heard of your victory.

409
00:39:07,520 --> 00:39:08,879
Congratulations my Bey.

410
00:39:10,560 --> 00:39:11,439
EyvAllah.

411
00:39:21,520 --> 00:39:22,919
Welcome my girl.

412
00:39:31,240 --> 00:39:32,719
Alps are ready Bala Hatun.

413
00:39:33,120 --> 00:39:34,439
Good.

414
00:39:36,120 --> 00:39:38,239
What is it? Who's leaving?

415
00:39:39,520 --> 00:39:40,359
I am.

416
00:39:44,120 --> 00:39:45,679
You said you'd stay.

417
00:39:47,120 --> 00:39:49,439
There are no trades with the lords.

418
00:39:50,200 --> 00:39:51,559
My duty is done.

419
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:56,639
It's time to leave.

420
00:39:57,920 --> 00:39:59,399
Take care of yourselves.

421
00:40:06,280 --> 00:40:07,799
Go safely Holofira.

422
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:09,839
Thank you.

423
00:40:15,720 --> 00:40:16,799
Come on Elcim.

424
00:40:33,240 --> 00:40:36,279
You were always like a mother to me Bala Hatun.

425
00:40:37,520 --> 00:40:38,799
I find it hard..

426
00:40:38,960 --> 00:40:41,079
...to be away from you.

427
00:40:43,480 --> 00:40:45,279
Mother can't be replaced.

428
00:40:45,520 --> 00:40:48,079
Holofira. I know that.

429
00:40:49,200 --> 00:40:52,359
A mother and a daughter always feels pain.

430
00:40:53,520 --> 00:40:55,079
But it gets better.

431
00:40:57,080 --> 00:40:59,999
You are like a daughter to me.

432
00:41:00,600 --> 00:41:02,119
My prayers will be with you.

433
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:05,839
Go safely.

434
00:41:07,320 --> 00:41:09,439
Thank you Mother Bala.

435
00:41:32,720 --> 00:41:34,479
Go safely lord's daughter.

436
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:38,119
May you go with speed...

437
00:41:40,360 --> 00:41:42,679
...and may angels protect you, I hope.

438
00:41:55,680 --> 00:41:58,279
You won't be here at the tribe for long.

439
00:42:01,160 --> 00:42:02,079
You will return...

440
00:42:03,800 --> 00:42:05,759
..in peace.

441
00:42:07,760 --> 00:42:11,159
Will you rage a war against us...

442
00:42:11,520 --> 00:42:13,599
...claiming it's your right?

443
00:42:17,200 --> 00:42:18,399
Frontier Market...

444
00:42:19,560 --> 00:42:21,439
...was Yakup Bey's.

445
00:42:21,920 --> 00:42:23,439
You took it.

446
00:42:24,880 --> 00:42:27,839
Mekece Castle was mine...

447
00:42:27,840 --> 00:42:29,839
...and you took it from me.

448
00:42:29,960 --> 00:42:32,119
When you do things like this...

449
00:42:32,120 --> 00:42:35,039
...how can there be peace?

450
00:42:37,280 --> 00:42:40,599
I won't let you have the frontier market.

451
00:42:40,960 --> 00:42:43,159
There is no more trade.

452
00:42:43,160 --> 00:42:44,479
It's over.

453
00:42:44,480 --> 00:42:46,679
You're going to go.

454
00:42:49,120 --> 00:42:50,799
Either on your foot...

455
00:42:52,480 --> 00:42:54,719
...or being carried in a carriage.

456
00:42:55,040 --> 00:42:59,919
You're going to pay
for what you've done, Osman Bey.

457
00:43:00,560 --> 00:43:03,639
I did everything I did for the unity of the Turks.

458
00:43:03,640 --> 00:43:05,039
But...

459
00:43:05,040 --> 00:43:07,559
...if you're going to stand against me...

460
00:43:07,560 --> 00:43:10,199
...if you're going to stop me...

461
00:43:10,200 --> 00:43:11,759
...then....

462
00:43:11,760 --> 00:43:14,679
...I won't forgive you again.

463
00:43:17,360 --> 00:43:19,399
Can I come in my bey?

464
00:43:19,600 --> 00:43:21,119
Come in.

465
00:43:23,920 --> 00:43:26,239
My bey an alp is here, he's injured.

466
00:43:26,800 --> 00:43:27,679
My bey.

467
00:43:27,680 --> 00:43:29,799
They took Gunduz Bey.

468
00:43:30,840 --> 00:43:32,199
Who?

469
00:43:32,600 --> 00:43:33,799
Byzantine.

470
00:43:33,800 --> 00:43:36,319
But they were different, my bey.

471
00:43:43,840 --> 00:43:45,919
Look at me.

472
00:43:48,160 --> 00:43:51,599
If you're involved in this...

473
00:43:55,760 --> 00:43:58,479
...you won't get to get out of here.

474
00:44:06,240 --> 00:44:07,999
Orhan, Alaeddin.

475
00:44:08,000 --> 00:44:09,999
Come with me.

476
00:44:14,920 --> 00:44:16,479
Orhan.

477
00:44:16,480 --> 00:44:18,119
My dad's alp is injured.

478
00:44:18,120 --> 00:44:19,239
Is there bad news?

479
00:44:19,240 --> 00:44:22,119
Gunduz Bey was ambushed Elcim.

480
00:44:24,760 --> 00:44:25,679
What?

481
00:44:39,720 --> 00:44:41,439
Hold on.

482
00:44:41,440 --> 00:44:45,399
Is he okay? Tell me the truth please.

483
00:44:46,400 --> 00:44:48,239
Come on alps.

484
00:44:48,240 --> 00:44:50,239
-I'll come too.
-Elcim.

485
00:44:50,240 --> 00:44:53,839
We don't have time. We're going
to bring your dad to you, I promise.

486
00:44:54,400 --> 00:44:55,999
Girl come.

487
00:44:56,000 --> 00:44:58,319
Orhan is right. Come on.

488
00:44:58,320 --> 00:45:01,239
We'll take care of her, come on.

489
00:45:04,360 --> 00:45:06,879
Whoever it is that has done this...

490
00:45:07,160 --> 00:45:09,639
...whoever it is that's behind this...

491
00:45:09,640 --> 00:45:12,279
This will be their last day alive.

492
00:45:14,640 --> 00:45:15,479
Come on.

493
00:45:28,200 --> 00:45:29,839
Come on.

494
00:45:37,000 --> 00:45:39,039
If Gunduz dies...

495
00:45:39,320 --> 00:45:42,199
...Osman will kill us all.

496
00:45:42,200 --> 00:45:45,279
He can't blame us for this too.

497
00:45:45,280 --> 00:45:47,679
I didn't do anything.

498
00:45:50,720 --> 00:45:52,919
That's it.

499
00:45:53,240 --> 00:45:56,079
Just like this you're going to die one by one.

500
00:45:56,080 --> 00:45:59,519
Everyday one of your
corpses will leave this tribe.

501
00:46:01,280 --> 00:46:03,679
Calm down.

502
00:46:03,840 --> 00:46:05,239
He's okay.

503
00:46:05,720 --> 00:46:07,239
He's okay.

504
00:46:10,480 --> 00:46:13,999
The only thing you can get from me is...

505
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:16,959
..blood and flesh.

506
00:46:17,400 --> 00:46:21,039
Even the ladies in our tribe...

507
00:46:21,040 --> 00:46:22,919
...hit harder than you.

508
00:46:41,600 --> 00:46:45,439
You don't know how to treat the captives Theodore.

509
00:46:45,640 --> 00:46:48,039
Look at Gunduz Bey.

510
00:46:48,560 --> 00:46:51,319
He's covered in blood.

511
00:46:51,640 --> 00:46:54,599
And there
is so many other ways to do this too.

512
00:46:54,600 --> 00:46:57,079
Isn't that so Gunduz Bey?

513
00:46:58,360 --> 00:47:00,159
Ulcay.

514
00:47:01,320 --> 00:47:03,159
Jackal.

515
00:47:05,680 --> 00:47:07,119
My only wish from Allah...

516
00:47:07,120 --> 00:47:10,959
Gunduz can't wish anymore.

517
00:47:13,760 --> 00:47:15,559
Gunduz...

518
00:47:15,560 --> 00:47:18,239
...has turned into a night now.

519
00:47:18,760 --> 00:47:22,279
You ran out of time now, Gunduz Bey.

520
00:47:26,880 --> 00:47:30,759
What are you waiting for then?

521
00:47:31,320 --> 00:47:35,479
Where we are going is clear.

522
00:47:35,960 --> 00:47:40,559
I will never give you what you want.

523
00:47:40,560 --> 00:47:45,399
You can think that. Things changed.

524
00:47:46,000 --> 00:47:53,559
Great emperor sent Konstantin
Paleologos as the protector of Rome.

525
00:47:54,080 --> 00:47:56,759
Your death..

526
00:47:57,600 --> 00:48:02,239
...will be a gift
of protection for Bursa.

527
00:48:02,720 --> 00:48:08,159
Battles require blood as payment.

528
00:48:09,760 --> 00:48:12,159
I am ready to pay for it.

529
00:48:12,400 --> 00:48:18,519
I swear that you won't die easily, Gunduz!

530
00:48:19,640 --> 00:48:23,039
What's on your mind, Ulcay?

531
00:48:24,400 --> 00:48:26,959
Osman must be after me.

532
00:48:27,280 --> 00:48:30,079
He will find my trace eventually.

533
00:48:30,360 --> 00:48:33,919
We will give him a gift first.

534
00:48:34,120 --> 00:48:39,919
While he is wasting his time with
the gift, we will go to Paleologos.

535
00:49:04,320 --> 00:49:06,559
Get out of the way, Gonca.

536
00:49:06,560 --> 00:49:08,639
Stop.

537
00:49:14,880 --> 00:49:20,359
So you hate me to the degree to
have me killed, huh Yakup Bey?

538
00:49:21,520 --> 00:49:23,039
What does that mean?

539
00:49:23,040 --> 00:49:26,959
I am talking about the Byzantine
soldiers you sent after the caravan.

540
00:49:27,280 --> 00:49:29,919
Did you not send them?

541
00:49:31,200 --> 00:49:33,799
Gonca.

542
00:49:37,320 --> 00:49:39,559
You...

543
00:49:40,800 --> 00:49:43,519
Were you in that caravan?

544
00:49:45,160 --> 00:49:47,599
Did you not know?

545
00:49:52,000 --> 00:49:54,559
Since you want to kill me...

546
00:49:55,040 --> 00:49:57,039
...I am right in front of you.

547
00:49:57,480 --> 00:50:02,799
Yakup Bey, you don't have
to send infidels behind me!

548
00:50:04,520 --> 00:50:08,999
When you slapped me, you set my heart on fire!

549
00:50:10,960 --> 00:50:14,159
You killed my love for you already.

550
00:50:15,040 --> 00:50:18,319
But it wasn't enough, huh?

551
00:50:21,480 --> 00:50:23,159
Okay.

552
00:50:23,960 --> 00:50:26,519
I am here.

553
00:50:27,000 --> 00:50:28,679
Come on.

554
00:50:29,920 --> 00:50:33,119
Draw your sword and kill me, Yakup Bey!

555
00:50:33,280 --> 00:50:36,559
My father wouldn't do that,
Gonca! Come to your senses!

556
00:50:39,840 --> 00:50:42,759
Am I lying?

557
00:50:43,240 --> 00:50:46,199
Did you not send them?

558
00:50:47,040 --> 00:50:48,479
We did.

559
00:50:59,200 --> 00:51:02,799
We established that
caravan together with Holofira.

560
00:51:03,520 --> 00:51:07,039
Everyone
knew that I would be in that caravan.

561
00:51:07,040 --> 00:51:08,199
But you did not?

562
00:51:08,200 --> 00:51:09,999
But...

563
00:51:10,960 --> 00:51:13,599
..but I did not know.

564
00:51:14,960 --> 00:51:16,759
I did not know.

565
00:51:16,760 --> 00:51:18,599
I wish...

566
00:51:19,520 --> 00:51:22,319
...I wish I could believe you.

567
00:51:26,320 --> 00:51:28,599
I would really want that.

568
00:51:38,640 --> 00:51:40,759
What are you talking about, dad?

569
00:51:43,720 --> 00:51:45,959
Melike Hatun said it.

570
00:51:47,680 --> 00:51:48,799
I guess...

571
00:51:50,040 --> 00:51:51,519
...all along...

572
00:51:52,040 --> 00:51:54,079
...she wanted Gonca to die.

573
00:52:00,320 --> 00:52:02,799
They were going to have me kill my girl.

574
00:52:35,000 --> 00:52:37,759
My Bey. They're Gunduz Bey's alps.

575
00:52:37,760 --> 00:52:38,719
Yes.

576
00:52:48,800 --> 00:52:51,159
My Bey. Boran Bey's coming.

577
00:52:57,200 --> 00:52:57,999
My Bey.

578
00:53:01,360 --> 00:53:03,239
We were moving with Ulcay.

579
00:53:04,760 --> 00:53:06,519
Byzantines showed up.

580
00:53:06,880 --> 00:53:08,879
They weren't regular soldiers.

581
00:53:10,800 --> 00:53:12,399
Ulcay went with them.

582
00:53:12,960 --> 00:53:16,359
He sent us to send word to
Germiyanids and Candarbeys.

583
00:53:18,880 --> 00:53:22,639
Bastard. Where did he go Konur?

584
00:53:24,640 --> 00:53:26,479
We'd follow him but...

585
00:53:26,480 --> 00:53:28,479
...we couldn't make it.

586
00:53:29,360 --> 00:53:32,719
Ulcay told us to go to Green Valley.

587
00:53:36,480 --> 00:53:37,519
Okay.

588
00:53:37,800 --> 00:53:40,359
They're after Gunduz Bey. They'll kill him.

589
00:53:40,840 --> 00:53:42,319
We can come my Bey.

590
00:53:42,600 --> 00:53:44,519
No.

591
00:53:44,600 --> 00:53:47,519
We must kill Ulcay today.

592
00:53:47,520 --> 00:53:49,919
You will go there as he said.

593
00:53:50,000 --> 00:53:52,119
We'll go after Gunduz Bey.

594
00:53:52,360 --> 00:53:53,879
As you wish my Bey.

595
00:53:55,040 --> 00:53:56,519
Give horses to Boran and Konur.

596
00:53:57,480 --> 00:53:58,919
Bury the martyrs.

597
00:53:59,440 --> 00:54:00,679
As you wish my Bey.

598
00:54:01,480 --> 00:54:02,679
Yes my Bey.

599
00:54:03,880 --> 00:54:04,719
Come.

600
00:54:21,560 --> 00:54:23,159
You have no mercy.

601
00:54:30,240 --> 00:54:32,359
You tied him up.

602
00:54:33,040 --> 00:54:37,239
He could be free one last time.

603
00:54:37,680 --> 00:54:39,679
Allah will punish you.

604
00:54:40,440 --> 00:54:42,319
You demons.

605
00:54:44,520 --> 00:54:46,479
Your evil..

606
00:54:47,040 --> 00:54:49,239
...won't make me obey you.

607
00:54:49,920 --> 00:54:50,799
Never.

608
00:54:51,440 --> 00:54:54,599
I like to bury men alive Theodoros.

609
00:54:56,200 --> 00:54:58,199
But it's different now.

610
00:54:58,320 --> 00:55:01,039
We'll play a game with Gunduz Bey.

611
00:55:02,640 --> 00:55:04,039
Right Gunduz Bey?

612
00:55:04,040 --> 00:55:07,679
You can't die just yet.

613
00:55:12,600 --> 00:55:14,039
Get him up.

614
00:55:21,480 --> 00:55:23,759
This will stop Osman...

615
00:55:25,480 --> 00:55:27,319
...and anger him Ulcay.

616
00:55:28,680 --> 00:55:29,559
I wish...

617
00:55:30,400 --> 00:55:33,559
...I could stay and see Osman's face.

618
00:56:04,880 --> 00:56:05,439
My Bey!

619
00:56:06,720 --> 00:56:09,879
There are traces.
They're new and alike.

620
00:56:10,240 --> 00:56:12,719
These tracks lead to north.

621
00:56:14,200 --> 00:56:16,079
They do it on purpose my Bey.

622
00:56:16,480 --> 00:56:18,639
They want to lead us where they want.

623
00:56:19,200 --> 00:56:22,039
All we can do is find Gunduz Bey.

624
00:56:24,880 --> 00:56:26,119
Osman Bey!

625
00:56:38,200 --> 00:56:39,439
Osman Bey!

626
00:56:41,400 --> 00:56:42,879
Osman Bey.

627
00:56:42,880 --> 00:56:43,879
Gunduz Bey.

628
00:56:43,880 --> 00:56:45,599
I'm here.

629
00:56:46,520 --> 00:56:48,719
Osman Bey.

630
00:56:54,400 --> 00:56:57,199
Bring the rope. Come on.

631
00:56:58,320 --> 00:57:01,119
Gunduz Bey, hold on.

632
00:57:08,240 --> 00:57:10,799
Come on alps, kids come on.

633
00:57:10,800 --> 00:57:12,439
Come on.

634
00:57:12,440 --> 00:57:14,919
Hold the rope Gunduz Bey.

635
00:57:15,080 --> 00:57:15,759
Hold it.

636
00:57:15,760 --> 00:57:16,799
Come on.

637
00:57:19,840 --> 00:57:21,839
Come on.

638
00:57:21,840 --> 00:57:25,639
We're going to fight so many on top
of our horses Gunduz Bey, hold on.

639
00:57:27,640 --> 00:57:28,199
Hold on.

640
00:57:28,200 --> 00:57:30,759
Come on.

641
00:57:32,520 --> 00:57:34,319
Oh Allah.

642
00:57:34,400 --> 00:57:36,639
Come on. Allah.

643
00:57:42,280 --> 00:57:44,039
Gunduz Bey.

644
00:57:44,720 --> 00:57:46,319
Are you okay?

645
00:57:47,120 --> 00:57:48,359
Are you?

646
00:57:48,360 --> 00:57:50,439
Osman Bey...

647
00:57:51,200 --> 00:57:54,879
Constantin, Paleologos...

648
00:57:54,880 --> 00:57:55,479
I know.

649
00:57:55,480 --> 00:57:56,639
Ulcay...

650
00:57:56,640 --> 00:57:57,919
I know.

651
00:57:57,920 --> 00:57:59,799
I know it all, don't worry.

652
00:57:59,800 --> 00:58:01,039
I know it all.

653
00:58:02,640 --> 00:58:05,119
Alaeddin come on help him.

654
00:58:05,280 --> 00:58:06,559
My bey.

655
00:58:07,160 --> 00:58:09,399
He's not doing okay.

656
00:58:12,680 --> 00:58:14,879
Give me some cloth.

657
00:58:16,120 --> 00:58:18,799
In the name
of Allah, the merciful, the beneficent.

658
00:58:19,480 --> 00:58:23,279
Hold on Gunduz Bey. Hold on.

659
00:58:28,920 --> 00:58:32,039
He will hold on, of course he will.

660
00:58:32,320 --> 00:58:34,399
Right Gunduz Bey?

661
00:58:34,400 --> 00:58:36,519
You are the rock behind our backs.

662
00:58:36,520 --> 00:58:38,599
Of course you will.

663
00:58:39,600 --> 00:58:42,679
Who will we trust then? Who?

664
00:58:42,960 --> 00:58:45,319
No, don't leave us alone.

665
00:58:45,320 --> 00:58:47,039
Come on.

666
00:58:47,040 --> 00:58:50,839
You're never alone Osman Bey.

667
00:58:51,720 --> 00:58:55,479
A whole nation stands with you.

668
00:58:55,800 --> 00:58:58,039
They stand behind you like a rock.

669
00:58:58,040 --> 00:59:00,119
I want you to see it too.

670
00:59:00,200 --> 00:59:02,079
You're going to see it too.

671
00:59:03,480 --> 00:59:07,319
...have to
give back the life that was trusted...

672
00:59:07,520 --> 00:59:10,439
...to me now Osman Bey.

673
00:59:12,000 --> 00:59:13,839
Elcim..

674
00:59:15,320 --> 00:59:16,999
I trust you...

675
00:59:20,160 --> 00:59:21,439
...and ...

676
00:59:21,920 --> 00:59:24,479
...you with her.

677
00:59:27,280 --> 00:59:29,919
My son Orhan.

678
00:59:31,680 --> 00:59:33,599
Don't worry.

679
00:59:33,800 --> 00:59:36,079
Don't worry Gunduz Bey.

680
00:59:42,320 --> 00:59:44,359
I will protect her with my life.

681
00:59:44,800 --> 00:59:47,919
I will protect her with my
life Gunduz Bey, don't worry.

682
00:59:49,760 --> 00:59:51,639
Take Bursa..

683
00:59:51,640 --> 00:59:54,159
...Osman Bey.

684
00:59:58,040 --> 00:59:59,999
Don't worry.

685
01:00:00,080 --> 01:00:02,199
I swear to Allah..

686
01:00:02,360 --> 01:00:03,719
...Bursa...

687
01:00:03,720 --> 01:00:05,599
...will be Turks' land, if Allah permits.

688
01:00:05,600 --> 01:00:07,559
If Allah permits.

689
01:00:09,720 --> 01:00:14,599
I bear witness that there is none
worthy of worship except Allah, and I ...

690
01:00:15,000 --> 01:00:24,519
...bear witness that
Mohammad is His servant and messenger.

691
01:00:34,160 --> 01:00:38,239
From Allah we came, to Him is our return.

692
01:00:40,600 --> 01:00:44,199
From Allah we came, to Him is our return.

693
01:01:08,800 --> 01:01:11,079
First, Gunduz Bey...

694
01:01:11,080 --> 01:01:12,799
...then...

695
01:01:13,440 --> 01:01:16,359
...everyone
from your household..

696
01:01:19,760 --> 01:01:21,799
Ulcay...

697
01:01:22,360 --> 01:01:24,599
Ulcay...

698
01:01:25,080 --> 01:01:28,439
Gunduz then everyone huh?

699
01:01:28,760 --> 01:01:30,919
I'm going to find you.

700
01:01:31,400 --> 01:01:32,679
This...

701
01:01:33,120 --> 01:01:36,079
...will be your last day.

702
01:01:36,080 --> 01:01:38,719
You won't live another day.

703
01:01:40,880 --> 01:01:43,959
I'm going to show you what it means to...

704
01:01:43,960 --> 01:01:48,439
...touch one of us.

705
01:02:18,400 --> 01:02:24,479
Gunduz Bey's kidnapping is not good.

706
01:02:26,840 --> 01:02:29,319
If anything happens to him...

707
01:02:29,320 --> 01:02:33,079
Osman will leave none of us alive.

708
01:02:33,800 --> 01:02:37,359
Are we going to stay for death here?

709
01:02:37,360 --> 01:02:39,319
Do something.

710
01:02:39,520 --> 01:02:43,079
Ibrahim Bey!

711
01:02:45,720 --> 01:02:49,279
Watch it, Yakup Bey!

712
01:02:51,600 --> 01:02:54,879
I will ask you only one question.

713
01:02:57,440 --> 01:03:03,319
When we
sent soldiers to stop Kayi's caravan...

714
01:03:03,600 --> 01:03:07,959
...did you know that Gonca was there?

715
01:03:21,800 --> 01:03:27,679
What are you implying, Yakup Bey?

716
01:03:30,160 --> 01:03:36,199
Did you send your soldiers
knowing that Gonca was there!?

717
01:03:41,600 --> 01:03:44,239
I did not know.

718
01:03:49,040 --> 01:03:51,559
Melike Hatun.

719
01:03:54,240 --> 01:03:56,959
Did you know?

720
01:04:02,240 --> 01:04:06,079
You almost made me kill my daughter!

721
01:04:06,480 --> 01:04:10,039
I did not know either, but...

722
01:04:11,080 --> 01:04:14,199
...did you not disown her?

723
01:04:15,440 --> 01:04:20,759
Does it matter her being in that caravan?

724
01:04:23,200 --> 01:04:24,359
You knew!

725
01:04:25,720 --> 01:04:29,959
You knew it, Melike
Hatun! You sent my sister to her death

726
01:04:30,600 --> 01:04:35,199
I did not know, don't you hear me?

727
01:04:36,240 --> 01:04:40,839
But weren't you going to kill that
girl who brought you disgrace?

728
01:04:40,840 --> 01:04:43,319
She is valuable now?

729
01:04:44,280 --> 01:04:49,239
She is my daughter! She is my blood!

730
01:04:52,560 --> 01:04:56,079
I am her father!

731
01:04:56,520 --> 01:04:58,919
Even with her...

732
01:04:59,480 --> 01:05:02,519
...mistakes and wrong doings, she is my daughter!

733
01:05:02,520 --> 01:05:04,919
Yakup Bey!

734
01:05:06,600 --> 01:05:10,519
Control yourself...

735
01:05:11,800 --> 01:05:14,359
...and your voice!

736
01:05:19,160 --> 01:05:22,639
I understand it now Ibrahim Bey.

737
01:05:23,680 --> 01:05:26,799
This is where we part ways

738
01:07:10,240 --> 01:07:11,079
Orhan.

739
01:07:48,920 --> 01:07:50,959
Father!

740
01:07:54,200 --> 01:07:57,879
Father!

741
01:08:00,840 --> 01:08:02,679
Who did it Osman Bey?

742
01:08:06,040 --> 01:08:07,839
Constantine Paleologos.

743
01:08:09,560 --> 01:08:10,319
He...

744
01:08:11,480 --> 01:08:13,719
...is working with Ulcay.

745
01:08:14,680 --> 01:08:17,158
We'll see him when we kill him.

746
01:08:28,520 --> 01:08:29,359
Elcim.

747
01:08:34,279 --> 01:08:36,158
We'll make them pay.

748
01:08:36,600 --> 01:08:38,078
I promise you.

749
01:08:38,680 --> 01:08:41,078
We'll make them pay.

750
01:08:51,920 --> 01:08:52,639
Bala.

751
01:08:53,520 --> 01:08:54,439
You should..

752
01:08:55,439 --> 01:08:57,799
...stay with Elcim. She's in pain.

753
01:08:58,200 --> 01:08:59,158
Support her.

754
01:08:59,160 --> 01:09:00,519
Don't worry.

755
01:09:01,600 --> 01:09:03,118
Father!

756
01:09:08,720 --> 01:09:10,679
My condolences Osman Bey.

757
01:09:13,880 --> 01:09:14,919
Gunduz..

758
01:09:15,560 --> 01:09:16,959
...was a brave Bey.

759
01:09:19,040 --> 01:09:20,198
My condolences.

760
01:09:22,479 --> 01:09:23,959
The man behind this...

761
01:09:25,720 --> 01:09:27,479
...was your soldier Ulcay.

762
01:09:29,920 --> 01:09:31,238
Ibrahim Bey.

763
01:09:38,880 --> 01:09:41,479
Why would Ulcay kill Gunduz Bey?

764
01:09:42,000 --> 01:09:44,959
The same reason why he killed our men...

765
01:09:45,399 --> 01:09:46,839
...all this time.

766
01:09:49,080 --> 01:09:51,038
What are you saying Osman Bey?

767
01:09:51,840 --> 01:09:53,559
I said it before.

768
01:09:53,720 --> 01:09:54,999
I'll say it again.

769
01:09:57,640 --> 01:09:59,639
If you were....

770
01:10:00,840 --> 01:10:02,999
..involved in this...

771
01:10:05,240 --> 01:10:06,319
...and if I prove it...

772
01:10:09,640 --> 01:10:11,359
...then I'll bury you in dirt.

773
01:10:26,600 --> 01:10:28,919
First I'll prove Ulcay did it.

774
01:10:30,440 --> 01:10:32,119
Then it's your turn.

775
01:11:08,880 --> 01:11:10,959
I won't cry until my father's killers...

776
01:11:12,320 --> 01:11:14,519
...are caught and punished.

777
01:11:17,520 --> 01:11:18,999
We won't cry now.

778
01:11:20,320 --> 01:11:21,919
I promise my Hatun.

779
01:11:23,000 --> 01:11:25,559
Those traitors will pay for it.

780
01:11:27,520 --> 01:11:29,399
Swords will talk now.

781
01:11:35,240 --> 01:11:36,559
Attention!

782
01:11:36,680 --> 01:11:37,719
Osman Bey!

783
01:11:52,400 --> 01:11:53,959
Girl.

784
01:11:54,280 --> 01:11:55,959
Are you feeling better?

785
01:11:56,080 --> 01:11:57,239
I am.

786
01:12:03,480 --> 01:12:05,479
Hold on girl.

787
01:12:05,720 --> 01:12:08,719
I hope Allah grants you patience.

788
01:12:09,280 --> 01:12:11,799
Thank you Bala Hatun.

789
01:12:13,560 --> 01:12:15,439
Osman Bey.

790
01:12:17,600 --> 01:12:18,839
Those who did this to my dad...

791
01:12:18,840 --> 01:12:20,599
Don't worry.

792
01:12:20,600 --> 01:12:22,879
They're going to pay for it.

793
01:12:23,280 --> 01:12:26,319
Ulcay and those Byzantine dogs who support him.

794
01:12:26,320 --> 01:12:29,039
We're going to end them all.

795
01:12:30,640 --> 01:12:34,079
When will we have the funeral my bey?

796
01:12:34,320 --> 01:12:36,639
Before Gunduz Bey's blood is dried...

797
01:12:36,640 --> 01:12:39,719
...that Ulcay will go into his grave.

798
01:12:41,520 --> 01:12:44,879
And we will fulfill our duty.

799
01:12:45,200 --> 01:12:47,119
Allow me...

800
01:12:47,400 --> 01:12:48,519
...to come.

801
01:12:48,520 --> 01:12:49,919
No.

802
01:12:50,240 --> 01:12:53,639
You will fulfill your last duty as well girl.

803
01:12:54,760 --> 01:12:58,479
Don't worry, we got it from here.

804
01:13:01,120 --> 01:13:03,839
We're going to take Gunduz Bey's revenge, Elcim.

805
01:13:03,840 --> 01:13:06,119
Don't worry.

806
01:13:16,400 --> 01:13:21,119
Osman ridiculed Candar and
Germiyan in front of the folk.

807
01:13:21,800 --> 01:13:25,279
Like that wasn't enough
he's keeping us in his tribe.

808
01:13:26,840 --> 01:13:31,879
Osman keeps his enemies
right in front of him Mehmet.

809
01:13:32,200 --> 01:13:34,919
What else does he have to
do that he keeps us here dad?

810
01:13:34,920 --> 01:13:37,239
He made us take the blame for his faults too.

811
01:13:37,240 --> 01:13:40,199
How will we get rid of this?

812
01:13:40,640 --> 01:13:42,239
When...

813
01:13:42,240 --> 01:13:45,919
...Osman reveals his intent...

814
01:13:46,000 --> 01:13:49,239
..we will make our move.

815
01:13:49,800 --> 01:13:51,559
But...

816
01:13:52,680 --> 01:13:55,639
...our unity with Ibrahim Bey...

817
01:13:55,760 --> 01:13:58,279
...has damaged us greatly.

818
01:13:59,600 --> 01:14:04,359
Their blind rage worked
in Osman's favor.

819
01:14:06,640 --> 01:14:09,359
There is no partnership no more.

820
01:14:11,320 --> 01:14:15,359
We're going to retake the leadership.

821
01:14:16,640 --> 01:14:19,239
Can I come in my bey?

822
01:14:19,240 --> 01:14:20,879
Come in.

823
01:14:25,440 --> 01:14:29,959
My bey, the Kayi alps want to enter the tent.

824
01:14:31,720 --> 01:14:33,359
Osman.

825
01:14:33,720 --> 01:14:35,719
Osman isn't sitting still dad.

826
01:14:35,720 --> 01:14:37,279
How can I?

827
01:14:37,280 --> 01:14:38,799
Let them in.

828
01:14:39,720 --> 01:14:41,999
Let's see what they have to say.

829
01:14:42,000 --> 01:14:44,079
As you wish my dad.

830
01:15:01,760 --> 01:15:04,159
Entering like...

831
01:15:04,160 --> 01:15:08,159
...you're attacking
at this hour, what does this mean Cerkutay?

832
01:15:10,680 --> 01:15:13,919
With Osman Bey's order...

833
01:15:19,520 --> 01:15:22,519
...we're going to take Mehmet Bey capture.

834
01:15:26,880 --> 01:15:29,479
Has Osman lost his mind?

835
01:15:29,480 --> 01:15:30,919
How dare he?

836
01:15:30,920 --> 01:15:33,959
Even patience has it's limits.

837
01:15:35,000 --> 01:15:38,319
Osman Bey's decision is final.

838
01:15:38,600 --> 01:15:42,399
To stop a war between the two beyhoods...

839
01:15:42,520 --> 01:15:44,399
...for a while...

840
01:15:44,840 --> 01:15:46,799
...Mehmet Bey will be our captive.

841
01:15:47,360 --> 01:15:48,559
Dad...

842
01:15:48,560 --> 01:15:50,639
...allow me to take his head off.

843
01:15:50,640 --> 01:15:52,239
Mehmet.

844
01:15:59,680 --> 01:16:02,959
Osman turned his back to you.

845
01:16:04,040 --> 01:16:07,159
I took care of you.

846
01:16:09,080 --> 01:16:11,319
Your son.

847
01:16:11,440 --> 01:16:13,119
Your family.

848
01:16:13,520 --> 01:16:15,719
You.

849
01:16:16,280 --> 01:16:19,759
I gave you a tent where you could live.

850
01:16:21,720 --> 01:16:25,559
You've shared your meals with Mehmet.

851
01:16:29,960 --> 01:16:32,839
And now are you going to take him?

852
01:16:40,800 --> 01:16:42,359
I will.

853
01:16:47,880 --> 01:16:49,719
Osman Bey...

854
01:16:49,840 --> 01:16:53,439
..never turned his back to me.

855
01:16:54,680 --> 01:16:56,839
His path was mine as well.

856
01:16:57,120 --> 01:16:58,839
My loyalty...

857
01:16:59,360 --> 01:17:01,999
...was always to him.

858
01:17:03,400 --> 01:17:06,199
Treacherous dog

859
01:17:14,760 --> 01:17:17,919
Mehmet's life is my care.

860
01:17:18,240 --> 01:17:20,399
If you don't make a mistake...

861
01:17:20,720 --> 01:17:23,839
...he won't be hurt, Yakup Bey.

862
01:17:23,840 --> 01:17:25,679
Excuse us.

863
01:17:26,320 --> 01:17:29,159
A fire fell onto Kayi tribe.

864
01:17:29,160 --> 01:17:31,279
Don't let it grow bigger.

865
01:17:34,560 --> 01:17:36,839
Mehmet, let go.

866
01:17:36,840 --> 01:17:38,159
Dad!

867
01:17:38,400 --> 01:17:40,799
Let go!

868
01:17:55,960 --> 01:17:59,279
If anything happens to Mehmet...

869
01:18:00,280 --> 01:18:04,399
...you will pay for it, Cerkutay!

870
01:18:05,240 --> 01:18:06,839
Beware!

871
01:18:08,080 --> 01:18:10,039
Alps.

872
01:18:10,360 --> 01:18:12,319
Take Mehmet Bey.

873
01:18:12,640 --> 01:18:14,439
Let go!

874
01:18:15,440 --> 01:18:20,119
Cerkutay, Osman will not get away with this!

875
01:18:54,280 --> 01:18:59,039
Speak Osman Bey.
Did you call us here to humiliate us?

876
01:18:59,800 --> 01:19:03,799
Mehmet Bey, let's listen to him first.

877
01:19:09,360 --> 01:19:11,279
Mehmet.

878
01:19:12,960 --> 01:19:15,799
Don't follow your father.

879
01:19:18,560 --> 01:19:21,239
When you stand behind me...

880
01:19:21,600 --> 01:19:24,159
...your fathers will stop.

881
01:19:24,160 --> 01:19:27,239
You are not keeping us as
prisoners just for this, right?

882
01:19:28,720 --> 01:19:31,359
You must have another goal.

883
01:19:35,360 --> 01:19:38,519
I will show you the truth.

884
01:19:39,040 --> 01:19:41,279
What truth.

885
01:19:42,560 --> 01:19:45,599
The truth that the enemies try to cover up.

886
01:19:45,600 --> 01:19:48,759
Don't you see us as your enemies, Osman Bey?

887
01:19:51,640 --> 01:19:54,559
If I saw you as enemies...

888
01:19:54,880 --> 01:19:57,199
...you wouldn't be here.

889
01:20:00,160 --> 01:20:05,119
Come on, get ready. We will depart at dawn.

890
01:20:27,280 --> 01:20:29,439
We are almost there.

891
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:33,079
I will continue alone.

892
01:20:33,320 --> 01:20:36,039
We should come with you for a little longer.

893
01:20:36,320 --> 01:20:39,239
Bursa soldiers shouldn't see you.

894
01:20:39,400 --> 01:20:41,279
Let's say our goodbyes here.

895
01:20:41,440 --> 01:20:43,159
Okay.

896
01:20:43,720 --> 01:20:45,799
Ulgen hatun.

897
01:20:46,160 --> 01:20:49,839
You always treat me like a big sister.

898
01:20:49,840 --> 01:20:52,359
Well, I did not do much.

899
01:20:53,400 --> 01:20:56,919
You were never happy ever
since you came to the tribe.

900
01:20:57,240 --> 01:20:59,559
I hope you will find peace in Bursa.

901
01:20:59,560 --> 01:21:02,959
I am glad for everything I
experienced together with Kayis.

902
01:21:02,960 --> 01:21:07,879
I wish my departure will be
the happy days for everyone.

903
01:21:08,560 --> 01:21:10,919
Ameen, if Allah permits.

904
01:21:16,480 --> 01:21:19,239
Come on!

905
01:21:48,680 --> 01:21:53,799
Allah Allah!

906
01:21:55,120 --> 01:21:57,839
Allah Allah!

907
01:22:00,640 --> 01:22:04,879
Tugay is nowhere to be found, Hatun.

908
01:22:06,360 --> 01:22:07,039
My Bey.

909
01:22:07,880 --> 01:22:09,039
Andra's gone too.

910
01:22:12,280 --> 01:22:13,479
Ibrahim Bey.

911
01:22:14,360 --> 01:22:16,599
They'll kill us all.

912
01:22:17,600 --> 01:22:19,319
And we're just waiting.

913
01:22:21,040 --> 01:22:22,759
May I come in Ibrahim Bey.

914
01:22:25,640 --> 01:22:26,599
Come.

915
01:22:33,840 --> 01:22:35,439
Bala Hatun expects you.

916
01:22:36,440 --> 01:22:37,919
Is that right?

917
01:22:38,040 --> 01:22:39,759
She's calling us?

918
01:22:41,960 --> 01:22:44,559
If Bala Hatun wants to speak...

919
01:22:45,760 --> 01:22:46,919
...she can come here.

920
01:22:48,400 --> 01:22:50,239
I won't go to anyone.

921
01:22:53,120 --> 01:22:54,759
Bala Hatun ordered me.

922
01:22:55,160 --> 01:22:57,199
You will go Ibrahim Bey.

923
01:22:58,760 --> 01:23:00,879
We could take you by force.

924
01:23:01,840 --> 01:23:04,199
But we'll do it. Just so you know.

925
01:23:07,160 --> 01:23:08,839
You really make us...

926
01:23:10,120 --> 01:23:12,239
...feel like captives.

927
01:23:22,440 --> 01:23:24,879
We'll have to go.

928
01:23:47,080 --> 01:23:48,599
Where were you Ulcay?

929
01:23:50,520 --> 01:23:53,799
I haven't been this happy in a long time.

930
01:23:55,200 --> 01:23:56,359
What is it?

931
01:23:57,760 --> 01:24:00,559
Kayi's great bey...

932
01:24:00,760 --> 01:24:01,959
...Gunduz.

933
01:24:02,880 --> 01:24:05,759
The land he called his own..

934
01:24:06,240 --> 01:24:08,719
..is now his grave.

935
01:24:09,640 --> 01:24:11,759
He died.

936
01:24:17,200 --> 01:24:18,719
Congratulations.

937
01:24:21,680 --> 01:24:22,719
What about Osman?

938
01:24:24,320 --> 01:24:25,599
Won't he follow us?

939
01:24:26,280 --> 01:24:27,599
Of course.

940
01:24:29,440 --> 01:24:30,879
But Osman..

941
01:24:31,800 --> 01:24:33,679
...is an injured wolf.

942
01:24:36,080 --> 01:24:37,799
We're not alone anymore.

943
01:24:39,440 --> 01:24:41,839
Constantine Paleologos.

944
01:24:42,280 --> 01:24:43,639
He's with us now.

945
01:24:44,240 --> 01:24:46,599
Soon he'll be here.

946
01:24:47,280 --> 01:24:48,599
I sent word.

947
01:24:50,720 --> 01:24:52,839
Who is Constantine?

948
01:24:53,240 --> 01:24:56,199
A man feared by even the
greatest Byzantine commanders.

949
01:24:57,280 --> 01:25:00,959
He massacred the lands
between Balkans and the east.

950
01:25:01,640 --> 01:25:04,599
He's only loyal to the Emperor.

951
01:25:09,440 --> 01:25:11,359
He'll be here now.

952
01:25:13,000 --> 01:25:14,159
Well...

953
01:25:14,800 --> 01:25:17,239
Osman wants war.

954
01:25:18,240 --> 01:25:20,999
And we'll do our part.

955
01:25:24,240 --> 01:25:28,039
We'll bring war to these lands.

956
01:25:28,760 --> 01:25:30,839
But first...

957
01:25:32,040 --> 01:25:35,719
...I'll kill Osman's family one by one.

958
01:25:41,320 --> 01:25:42,839
How will we do it?

959
01:25:43,880 --> 01:25:44,839
You'll see.

960
01:25:55,560 --> 01:25:58,119
Constantine Paleologos.

961
01:25:58,760 --> 01:26:01,599
Now we know who to attack.

962
01:26:01,800 --> 01:26:03,799
That bastard.

963
01:26:04,040 --> 01:26:06,239
He was a snake.

964
01:26:06,720 --> 01:26:09,279
Ibrahim Bey will kill him.

965
01:26:09,800 --> 01:26:11,079
Hold on.

966
01:26:11,520 --> 01:26:13,159
You didn't hear everything yet.

967
01:26:14,080 --> 01:26:16,679
These are only words.

968
01:26:17,120 --> 01:26:19,279
Now it's time for arrogance.

969
01:26:20,440 --> 01:26:22,559
You'll hear everything.

970
01:26:23,240 --> 01:26:24,439
Everything.

971
01:26:29,920 --> 01:26:31,559
Bala Hatun.

972
01:26:32,280 --> 01:26:36,639
You made us come here. What's so urgent?

973
01:26:38,440 --> 01:26:40,839
Have a seat Ibrahim Bey.

974
01:26:40,840 --> 01:26:41,719
Here.

975
01:26:42,000 --> 01:26:44,879
You made us come here.

976
01:26:44,880 --> 01:26:46,879
And now you order us.

977
01:26:46,960 --> 01:26:48,359
We have no time to sit.

978
01:26:49,440 --> 01:26:51,679
What will you speak about?

979
01:26:52,280 --> 01:26:54,639
All you do is talk since we got here.

980
01:26:54,840 --> 01:26:57,959
-But it's all nonsense!
-Either you don't hear me...

981
01:26:57,960 --> 01:26:59,959
...or you don't understand,
Melike Hatun.

982
01:27:00,760 --> 01:27:01,919
Bala Hatun.

983
01:27:03,680 --> 01:27:06,999
Tell me what's important.

984
01:27:10,520 --> 01:27:14,119
Gonca, it looks a bit dark in here right?

985
01:27:14,120 --> 01:27:19,079
Can you go and light those up?
Let us see each other more clearly.

986
01:27:21,680 --> 01:27:23,519
Okay mother.

987
01:27:44,280 --> 01:27:47,839
I'm running out of patience Bala Hatun.

988
01:27:48,040 --> 01:27:49,719
Come to the conclusion.

989
01:27:49,720 --> 01:27:51,319
Osman Bey.

990
01:27:51,320 --> 01:27:54,479
He went to get
Ulcay, Ibrahim Bey.

991
01:27:54,560 --> 01:27:58,079
About that fake judge thing.

992
01:27:59,200 --> 01:28:00,879
Bala Hatun.

993
01:28:01,240 --> 01:28:04,119
I've told Osman Bey this too.

994
01:28:04,120 --> 01:28:08,999
We have nothing to do with this fake judge.

995
01:28:09,000 --> 01:28:11,319
Why are you still asking this?

996
01:28:11,320 --> 01:28:17,879
Then you must not know that the fake
judge was from your lands, Ibrahim Bey.

997
01:28:22,640 --> 01:28:28,919
And he was punished because
he was unfair in his cases.

998
01:28:29,800 --> 01:28:34,399
What
are you two trying to say right now?

999
01:28:34,400 --> 01:28:36,479
What are you saying?

1000
01:28:36,480 --> 01:28:38,639
Ibrahim Bey, let's go.

1001
01:28:38,640 --> 01:28:42,719
Hold on Melike Hatun.

1002
01:28:43,080 --> 01:28:45,679
We're talking here.

1003
01:28:46,720 --> 01:28:49,359
Why are you scared of?

1004
01:28:49,760 --> 01:28:51,839
Your lies...

1005
01:28:51,840 --> 01:28:54,199
..or your sins?

1006
01:28:54,560 --> 01:28:59,799
Didn't you kill
Rukneddin The Judge to get my son killed?

1007
01:29:01,360 --> 01:29:05,199
Hold on there.

1008
01:29:05,640 --> 01:29:07,839
What are you saying Bala Hatun?

1009
01:29:10,320 --> 01:29:11,839
Melike.

1010
01:29:12,080 --> 01:29:14,039
Think about it Ibrahim Bey.

1011
01:29:14,040 --> 01:29:14,999
Think.

1012
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:17,159
The court ending quickly.

1013
01:29:17,160 --> 01:29:20,199
Alaeddin being punished by death.

1014
01:29:20,200 --> 01:29:22,639
Who else would want that apart from you?

1015
01:29:22,640 --> 01:29:24,919
Even if it's not you...

1016
01:29:25,360 --> 01:29:27,199
...then his mother.

1017
01:29:29,680 --> 01:29:33,759
She's lying.

1018
01:29:33,760 --> 01:29:36,279
You took my son's life first...

1019
01:29:36,280 --> 01:29:39,759
...and now you're trying to get in between us.

1020
01:29:40,480 --> 01:29:42,799
I won't stay here longer.

1021
01:29:42,800 --> 01:29:45,039
Ibrahim Bey let's go.

1022
01:29:45,040 --> 01:29:48,079
That's not it either, Melike Hatun.

1023
01:29:48,280 --> 01:29:49,639
I've heard it.

1024
01:29:50,080 --> 01:29:53,399
You've looked into the witches near here.

1025
01:29:56,200 --> 01:30:01,679
How can you try to do something
that Allah has made a sin?

1026
01:30:02,920 --> 01:30:04,399
Melike.

1027
01:30:04,400 --> 01:30:07,199
Your lies never end.

1028
01:30:07,360 --> 01:30:09,879
I won't stay here anymore. Move.

1029
01:30:09,880 --> 01:30:12,919
Fearing for your life Melike Hatun?

1030
01:30:16,280 --> 01:30:17,639
Don't be scared.

1031
01:30:17,640 --> 01:30:18,559
You won't die.

1032
01:30:18,560 --> 01:30:19,119
Let go.

1033
01:30:19,120 --> 01:30:22,719
Not just Rukneddin The Judge, Ibrahim Bey.

1034
01:30:22,840 --> 01:30:27,039
Your wife placed a poisoned candle in our room...

1035
01:30:27,040 --> 01:30:29,959
...and tried to kill us too.

1036
01:30:29,960 --> 01:30:32,399
We heard it from the witch she went to.

1037
01:30:33,160 --> 01:30:35,239
Don't be scared.

1038
01:30:35,240 --> 01:30:37,639
She got her punishment as well.

1039
01:31:03,400 --> 01:31:05,319
Osman.

1040
01:31:06,440 --> 01:31:10,279
Did you think that the wolf
wouldn't smell the scent of the jackal?

1041
01:31:11,560 --> 01:31:14,919
If you tried to trick one of us...

1042
01:31:14,920 --> 01:31:17,159
But that's how things work.

1043
01:31:18,840 --> 01:31:21,439
Jackal set up a trap...

1044
01:31:21,440 --> 01:31:23,439
...and you fall for it.

1045
01:31:23,640 --> 01:31:26,079
Look? That's the case again.

1046
01:31:50,520 --> 01:31:54,119
Just in time beys.

1047
01:32:04,400 --> 01:32:06,599
First Gunduz...

1048
01:32:06,760 --> 01:32:08,159
...then you.

1049
01:32:08,800 --> 01:32:10,399
You can't run Osman.

1050
01:32:11,880 --> 01:32:14,519
We won't escape, huh?

1051
01:32:16,600 --> 01:32:19,399
Who says we are afraid of death?

1052
01:32:19,640 --> 01:32:23,079
We live with death!

1053
01:32:24,120 --> 01:32:27,959
Did Gunduz Bey beg you?

1054
01:32:28,280 --> 01:32:31,919
Either by begging, or bravely.

1055
01:32:32,120 --> 01:32:35,319
You can't change the truth.

1056
01:32:36,520 --> 01:32:41,959
This time, you can't do anything.

1057
01:32:44,120 --> 01:32:46,759
I set up the trap for you Osman.

1058
01:32:47,240 --> 01:32:51,879
I knew you would follow
me. I took all the precautions.

1059
01:32:51,880 --> 01:32:53,159
All the precautions.

1060
01:32:55,640 --> 01:32:58,399
First, you lost to your ambition...

1061
01:32:58,400 --> 01:33:01,479
...and now you will lose to me!

1062
01:33:06,040 --> 01:33:08,759
I killed Ahmet.

1063
01:33:13,400 --> 01:33:17,399
I raided Karacahisar market.

1064
01:33:19,200 --> 01:33:23,119
I killed the judge with my own hands!

1065
01:33:30,440 --> 01:33:33,439
Now I will kill you.

1066
01:33:36,360 --> 01:33:41,279
Even the sheytaan couldn't
think of the things this bastard did!

1067
01:33:41,280 --> 01:33:43,719
Let's go and kill him

1068
01:33:43,760 --> 01:33:45,959
Stop, Mehmet Bey.

1069
01:33:46,240 --> 01:33:47,639
Let him finish.

1070
01:33:47,640 --> 01:33:49,639
Control yourself, Mehmet.

1071
01:33:50,240 --> 01:33:54,039
It looks like we have more to hear.

1072
01:33:59,560 --> 01:34:04,279
How could you do this, Hatun?

1073
01:34:04,960 --> 01:34:07,959
Did you really kill dear judge?

1074
01:34:07,960 --> 01:34:10,439
How could I know, my Bey?

1075
01:34:10,440 --> 01:34:14,399
How could I know that
the murderer of our son is a Byzantian...

1076
01:34:14,399 --> 01:34:15,619
Shut up!

1077
01:34:16,760 --> 01:34:18,799
Shut up!

1078
01:34:20,640 --> 01:34:24,999
You brought me disgrace! Shut up.

1079
01:34:25,640 --> 01:34:28,319
I don't want to hear you.

1080
01:34:28,680 --> 01:34:30,959
Our son's killer is found!

1081
01:34:30,960 --> 01:34:32,319
No.

1082
01:34:32,720 --> 01:34:35,959
Ibrahim Bey, he wasn't the killer.

1083
01:34:35,960 --> 01:34:38,159
What are you saying, Bala Hatun?

1084
01:34:38,360 --> 01:34:39,879
He was!

1085
01:34:40,320 --> 01:34:41,839
That Byzantine man

1086
01:34:41,840 --> 01:34:44,359
The scheme is greater than that.

1087
01:34:45,360 --> 01:34:49,879
The killer of your son that dog called Ulcay.

1088
01:34:52,960 --> 01:34:57,399
Someone else was holding
his leash. It was all his plan.

1089
01:34:58,080 --> 01:35:01,239
He wants
to make Turkmens fight each other.

1090
01:35:02,040 --> 01:35:04,559
Osman Bey is after him now.

1091
01:35:05,200 --> 01:35:07,919
He will catch that trickster.

1092
01:35:08,840 --> 01:35:11,799
Ulcay.

1093
01:35:12,640 --> 01:35:17,519
Do you know what I am going
to do after I kill you and your son?

1094
01:35:19,280 --> 01:35:21,399
I will...

1095
01:35:22,400 --> 01:35:27,039
...place Germiyan and Candar flags here!

1096
01:35:32,280 --> 01:35:37,039
You act with Olcaytu's orders
and try to devise a scheme, huh?

1097
01:35:37,200 --> 01:35:41,559
The Turks who hear
this won't be able to get united again.

1098
01:35:41,800 --> 01:35:43,359
Osman.

1099
01:35:45,080 --> 01:35:47,319
Your dreams will not com true.

1100
01:35:47,480 --> 01:35:50,319
If you acted on your own...

1101
01:35:50,520 --> 01:35:53,919
...you would
realize that this is not just my cause.

1102
01:35:54,240 --> 01:35:58,279
But you couldn't comprehend that.

1103
01:35:59,040 --> 01:36:03,159
Now, if my flag falls...,

1104
01:36:03,400 --> 01:36:06,799
...you will see that others will pick it up.

1105
01:36:06,800 --> 01:36:08,199
Olcaytu will see it too!

1106
01:36:08,200 --> 01:36:10,079
I will kill whoever picks it up, too!

1107
01:36:13,400 --> 01:36:16,119
The land and the sky belongs to us!

1108
01:36:16,520 --> 01:36:22,519
As long as Ilkhanid Empire
lives, only their flag flies!

1109
01:36:26,040 --> 01:36:28,599
I will crush you now.

1110
01:36:33,720 --> 01:36:35,719
But...

1111
01:36:36,560 --> 01:36:38,559
...I will do it alone.

1112
01:36:46,360 --> 01:36:47,879
Come here.

1113
01:37:07,560 --> 01:37:09,439
I came here for two things.

1114
01:37:10,200 --> 01:37:11,959
First, what you'll confess.

1115
01:37:12,400 --> 01:37:15,599
And your worthless body.

1116
01:37:47,320 --> 01:37:48,559
Attack!

1117
01:38:03,280 --> 01:38:04,319
We're here my Bey.

1118
01:38:04,800 --> 01:38:06,999
Allah is the Greatest!

1119
01:38:16,600 --> 01:38:17,639
Konur!

1120
01:38:18,280 --> 01:38:19,799
Konur let's go!

1121
01:38:43,680 --> 01:38:44,239
My Bey.

1122
01:38:46,800 --> 01:38:48,079
Ibrahim Bey.

1123
01:38:57,560 --> 01:38:58,399
Ibrahim.

1124
01:39:00,280 --> 01:39:02,559
Don't believe them.

1125
01:39:02,560 --> 01:39:03,879
Shut up

1126
01:39:10,880 --> 01:39:12,359
What have you done?

1127
01:39:15,440 --> 01:39:17,319
What have you done Hatun?

1128
01:39:20,040 --> 01:39:21,479
Did you do sorcery?

1129
01:39:23,000 --> 01:39:24,679
Did you kill the Great Turk...

1130
01:39:25,680 --> 01:39:28,119
...Rukneddin The Judge?

1131
01:39:31,440 --> 01:39:34,079
I did it out of pain my Bey.

1132
01:39:36,360 --> 01:39:37,559
I did it...

1133
01:39:38,680 --> 01:39:40,159
...because I was in pain.

1134
01:39:40,160 --> 01:39:42,159
Shut up!

1135
01:39:54,920 --> 01:39:57,639
You are full of sin.

1136
01:40:07,320 --> 01:40:09,639
I won't let you get away with it.

1137
01:40:11,960 --> 01:40:13,999
You'll pay for it.

1138
01:40:14,880 --> 01:40:16,359
But...

1139
01:40:16,440 --> 01:40:17,999
...until we go back home...

1140
01:40:19,680 --> 01:40:21,679
...you won't make another mistake.

1141
01:40:25,360 --> 01:40:26,599
Ibrahim Bey.

1142
01:40:29,000 --> 01:40:30,199
Bala.

1143
01:40:31,640 --> 01:40:33,839
I won't let you get away with it.

1144
01:41:09,480 --> 01:41:13,159
This is the lands boys become men

1145
01:41:13,160 --> 01:41:16,079
We'll before dogs take over!

1146
01:41:17,520 --> 01:41:20,039
Oh Allah!

1147
01:41:35,120 --> 01:41:36,959
Gunduz Bey has just died.

1148
01:41:37,360 --> 01:41:39,719
And I'll kill
you for it Theodore.

1149
01:41:39,720 --> 01:41:40,919
Come here.

1150
01:41:45,560 --> 01:41:48,119
Soldiers! Soldiers!

1151
01:41:48,160 --> 01:41:49,559
What is it?

1152
01:41:49,560 --> 01:41:51,839
Are you actually not that brave?

1153
01:42:00,160 --> 01:42:02,479
Revenge is swiftly held with us Theodore.

1154
01:42:03,960 --> 01:42:05,759
Now...

1155
01:42:07,720 --> 01:42:09,759
...Gunduz Bey will rest in peace.

1156
01:42:09,760 --> 01:42:12,239
You killing me will change nothing.

1157
01:42:12,240 --> 01:42:14,279
Constantine is coming for you.

1158
01:42:14,280 --> 01:42:16,679
Let him, it doesn't matter.

1159
01:42:16,680 --> 01:42:18,919
The only place he will go....

1160
01:42:22,680 --> 01:42:24,599
...is hell.

1161
01:42:33,320 --> 01:42:37,799
Konur, you traitor.
I should've known.

1162
01:42:40,600 --> 01:42:44,479
What were you when you
infiltrating Ibrahim Bey's people?

1163
01:42:44,720 --> 01:42:47,079
You lowlife dog.

1164
01:42:51,440 --> 01:42:54,639
Did you think we wouldn't know that you would run?

1165
01:43:04,160 --> 01:43:07,519
I was never loyal to you Ulcay.

1166
01:43:07,760 --> 01:43:11,039
You were my hardest duty, Ulcay.

1167
01:43:11,440 --> 01:43:12,759
Get up.

1168
01:43:14,400 --> 01:43:17,119
Move.

1169
01:43:17,880 --> 01:43:19,359
Move.

1170
01:43:31,160 --> 01:43:32,959
Move!

1171
01:43:35,360 --> 01:43:37,359
Here...

1172
01:43:38,080 --> 01:43:42,199
...is the one has concealed
the truth and changed it.

1173
01:43:42,320 --> 01:43:43,759
Now...

1174
01:43:43,760 --> 01:43:45,639
...we're going to take him to the tribe.

1175
01:43:45,640 --> 01:43:47,799
So that...

1176
01:43:47,800 --> 01:43:50,239
...the beys can see him too.

1177
01:43:50,640 --> 01:43:55,799
We saw the reason and the result
of your patience, Osman Bey. Thank you.

1178
01:43:56,800 --> 01:43:59,199
Thank you, Osman Bey.

1179
01:44:01,640 --> 01:44:04,119
Think of me as a father now.

1180
01:44:05,160 --> 01:44:07,879
We didn't think
of you as other but as one of our own.

1181
01:44:12,920 --> 01:44:14,119
Move now.

1182
01:44:14,480 --> 01:44:15,759
Move.

1183
01:44:24,240 --> 01:44:26,039
Osman Bey was right.

1184
01:44:26,040 --> 01:44:30,279
It was clear that he was but we
resisted not to see it Mehmet Bey.

1185
01:44:30,440 --> 01:44:32,199
That Ulcay...

1186
01:44:32,200 --> 01:44:34,199
He fooled us all this time.

1187
01:44:34,200 --> 01:44:36,719
Lowlife scum.

1188
01:44:55,000 --> 01:44:57,926
Friend of Kayis who
enslaved me and released me

1189
01:44:57,938 --> 01:45:00,999
in exchange of slave Turks
thus embarrassing me...

1190
01:45:01,000 --> 01:45:02,959
...Princess Holofira.

1191
01:45:02,960 --> 01:45:05,959
How dare you come-here?

1192
01:45:06,480 --> 01:45:08,479
Commander Alexius.

1193
01:45:08,480 --> 01:45:10,239
Please allow me to explain.

1194
01:45:10,240 --> 01:45:11,679
Explain

1195
01:45:11,680 --> 01:45:15,239
Are you going to explain how you
worked with our arch nemesis Turks?

1196
01:45:15,240 --> 01:45:16,919
Explain it.

1197
01:45:16,920 --> 01:45:18,159
Never.

1198
01:45:18,160 --> 01:45:21,119
I would never work with them Commander.

1199
01:45:22,920 --> 01:45:27,919
I am just a sinner who
has faced the Turks' wrath.

1200
01:45:30,440 --> 01:45:32,319
Orhan.

1201
01:45:34,040 --> 01:45:36,039
He made me believe his love...

1202
01:45:36,040 --> 01:45:38,559
...and then married a Turk.

1203
01:45:38,560 --> 01:45:40,239
Not a friend..

1204
01:45:40,240 --> 01:45:42,679
...but I'm their biggest enemy.

1205
01:45:43,880 --> 01:45:50,279
Do you think that we won't make you pay for
the foolishness of believing in a Turk's love?

1206
01:45:50,400 --> 01:45:52,679
Why are you,here?

1207
01:45:54,440 --> 01:45:57,199
Please don't throw my sin in my face, Commander.

1208
01:45:57,200 --> 01:45:59,799
Allow me to beg for
forgiveness from Jesus Christ...

1209
01:45:59,800 --> 01:46:01,999
...and be of your service till I die.

1210
01:46:02,000 --> 01:46:04,919
Allow me to stay at the Monastery.

1211
01:46:05,760 --> 01:46:10,159
A sinner like you in a Monastery?

1212
01:46:10,360 --> 01:46:12,759
I would've killed you a long
time ago if it was up to me.

1213
01:46:12,760 --> 01:46:17,359
But Constantine will make the decision about you.

1214
01:46:21,400 --> 01:46:25,079
Until Commander Constantine is here,
she will stay in the dungeons. Take her.

1215
01:46:35,640 --> 01:46:36,359
Move.

1216
01:46:36,360 --> 01:46:38,239
-Killer.
-Move.

1217
01:46:38,240 --> 01:46:41,119
-Move.
-You killer.

1218
01:46:41,120 --> 01:46:42,959
-Move.
-Traitor.

1219
01:46:42,960 --> 01:46:45,519
-Kill him.
-Killer.

1220
01:46:50,520 --> 01:46:53,279
Move!

1221
01:47:01,880 --> 01:47:03,599
Move!

1222
01:47:06,680 --> 01:47:11,919
Gunduz Bey has become a
martyr and reached the afterlife...

1223
01:47:12,200 --> 01:47:15,719
...but you will go to hell, you bastard!

1224
01:47:15,720 --> 01:47:18,119
Stop.

1225
01:47:20,280 --> 01:47:25,119
Solgur Aga.

1226
01:47:28,400 --> 01:47:29,759
Traitor!

1227
01:47:29,760 --> 01:47:31,879
Move!

1228
01:47:41,640 --> 01:47:43,359
Move!

1229
01:47:56,560 --> 01:47:58,919
Elcim.

1230
01:47:59,760 --> 01:48:01,959
My father will do what's necessary.

1231
01:48:11,160 --> 01:48:15,879
It was all because of you.

1232
01:48:16,200 --> 01:48:18,079
Dervish.

1233
01:48:18,160 --> 01:48:22,679
It's the great
Allah who starts and finishes everything.

1234
01:48:23,560 --> 01:48:25,079
We will return to him eventually.

1235
01:48:25,080 --> 01:48:26,239
We-will return to him'eventually.

1236
01:48:26,880 --> 01:48:30,999
What really matters is how
we are going to return to him.

1237
01:48:31,480 --> 01:48:33,559
With dignity, or a black heart?

1238
01:48:34,040 --> 01:48:38,679
Either hell or heaven.

1239
01:48:40,240 --> 01:48:44,799
This tribe will become your hell.

1240
01:48:46,320 --> 01:48:51,399
People should know what lies behind
their words, and shouldn't speak ill words.

1241
01:48:51,840 --> 01:48:56,959
In this hell of a world, words can kill.

1242
01:49:02,800 --> 01:49:05,799
Move now!
Move!

1243
01:49:09,240 --> 01:49:10,959
Move!

1244
01:49:16,520 --> 01:49:18,359
Come here!

1245
01:49:25,240 --> 01:49:27,399
This jackal...

1246
01:49:27,920 --> 01:49:31,959
...everyone
thought of him as Ibrahim Bey's man!

1247
01:49:32,280 --> 01:49:37,119
But in truth, he served fitna, cruelty...

1248
01:49:37,120 --> 01:49:40,199
...and Olcaytu

1249
01:49:54,200 --> 01:49:56,919
He worked with Byzantine!

1250
01:49:57,480 --> 01:50:00,759
Whoever stood against us...

1251
01:50:01,400 --> 01:50:04,159
...he worked with them!

1252
01:50:07,040 --> 01:50:11,599
Our kin did not do something different either.

1253
01:50:19,120 --> 01:50:23,079
This dog killed Rukneddin The Judge!

1254
01:50:23,400 --> 01:50:25,279
And...

1255
01:50:26,760 --> 01:50:29,479
...he killed Ahmet Bey!

1256
01:50:31,160 --> 01:50:33,359
Is that right?

1257
01:50:35,200 --> 01:50:36,959
Is that right, Ulcay!?

1258
01:50:36,960 --> 01:50:40,199
Ask your sons.

1259
01:50:40,480 --> 01:50:42,759
Tell your Beys about it.

1260
01:50:43,280 --> 01:50:44,759
Is that right, Mehmet?

1261
01:50:44,760 --> 01:50:46,599
That's right, father.

1262
01:50:47,840 --> 01:50:50,079
He confessed it himself.

1263
01:50:51,440 --> 01:50:54,559
He took part in Gunduz Bey's death too.

1264
01:50:57,080 --> 01:51:01,959
I fed you for years! And you killed Ahmed

1265
01:51:02,320 --> 01:51:05,039
What did you want from Ahmed

1266
01:51:05,400 --> 01:51:07,799
You bastard!

1267
01:51:08,120 --> 01:51:11,159
Why didn't you kill me!?

1268
01:51:15,600 --> 01:51:19,679
Stop there, Ibrahim Bey.

1269
01:51:20,160 --> 01:51:23,679
Your scale of justice was never right.

1270
01:51:23,680 --> 01:51:27,359
You never accepted the truth.

1271
01:51:27,520 --> 01:51:31,959
That's why, you can't bring the justice!

1272
01:51:32,680 --> 01:51:37,079
Beys, calm down.

1273
01:51:39,000 --> 01:51:41,639
We spent lots of time together, right?

1274
01:51:44,600 --> 01:51:46,999
Well, first of all...

1275
01:51:47,360 --> 01:51:52,039
...you raided Karacahisar market, right?

1276
01:51:52,520 --> 01:51:54,559
Tell them about it.

1277
01:51:59,040 --> 01:52:01,399
Ulcay's not the only sinner.

1278
01:52:01,640 --> 01:52:03,199
Not true.

1279
01:52:03,720 --> 01:52:04,959
Shut up!

1280
01:52:12,080 --> 01:52:13,679
Osman Bey!

1281
01:52:14,520 --> 01:52:16,079
Before he dies..

1282
01:52:16,680 --> 01:52:19,119
..he wants to cause chaos.

1283
01:52:22,200 --> 01:52:26,999
We have nothing to do with a market raid.

1284
01:52:27,920 --> 01:52:31,639
Ulcay Wants to slander our name.

1285
01:52:33,960 --> 01:52:35,399
...were born men...

1286
01:52:36,520 --> 01:52:37,999
...but we die a jackal.

1287
01:52:39,320 --> 01:52:41,519
You will always...

1288
01:52:42,120 --> 01:52:44,039
..be snakes.

1289
01:52:46,840 --> 01:52:48,039
And you...

1290
01:52:48,680 --> 01:52:50,439
...worked with Ulcay.

1291
01:52:50,760 --> 01:52:53,399
Olcaytu's orders...

1292
01:52:53,680 --> 01:52:55,959
...led you to sin against us.

1293
01:52:56,640 --> 01:52:58,759
You wanted us to kill each other.

1294
01:52:59,200 --> 01:53:01,279
We always stopped that.

1295
01:53:01,800 --> 01:53:02,559
Why?

1296
01:53:03,120 --> 01:53:04,959
So we won't kill our brothers.

1297
01:53:06,640 --> 01:53:07,719
This dog will die here.

1298
01:53:08,360 --> 01:53:11,879
And you'll get the hell out of my lands.

1299
01:53:12,480 --> 01:53:13,479
Osman Bey.

1300
01:53:14,680 --> 01:53:18,679
You won't even let me kill my son's killer.

1301
01:53:18,880 --> 01:53:21,879
You're the ones who brought
these bastards to our land.

1302
01:53:24,120 --> 01:53:28,479
Despite that, we don't make you pay for it.

1303
01:53:29,240 --> 01:53:30,159
Know that...

1304
01:53:31,760 --> 01:53:33,759
..it's out of mercy.

1305
01:53:34,880 --> 01:53:35,879
It's because...

1306
01:53:36,680 --> 01:53:39,079
...we don't kill our brothers.

1307
01:53:43,440 --> 01:53:44,399
Osman Bey.

1308
01:53:45,200 --> 01:53:48,159
As long as you have snakes around you...

1309
01:53:48,960 --> 01:53:50,879
...you don't need another enemy.

1310
01:53:50,920 --> 01:53:52,079
Shut up!

1311
01:53:56,040 --> 01:53:58,519
If dogs like you never came to our land...

1312
01:53:58,600 --> 01:54:01,999
...no one would deceit our men.

1313
01:54:02,960 --> 01:54:03,959
From now on..

1314
01:54:04,400 --> 01:54:07,039
...we won't work to convince traitors.

1315
01:54:10,320 --> 01:54:13,559
Nicea and Bursa will be under siege.

1316
01:54:15,920 --> 01:54:20,239
The oppressor's land will be ours.

1317
01:54:20,760 --> 01:54:22,039
And this dog...

1318
01:54:23,760 --> 01:54:25,559
...will be eaten by birds.

1319
01:54:30,600 --> 01:54:31,999
Yunus Emre..-.

1320
01:54:33,280 --> 01:54:34,959
...said it perfectly.

1321
01:54:36,720 --> 01:54:38,359
An eye for an eye.

1322
01:54:40,000 --> 01:54:41,159
This dog will die...

1323
01:54:43,440 --> 01:54:45,279
...will die like Ahmet Bey.

1324
01:54:50,720 --> 01:54:53,439
Our only rule...

1325
01:54:54,440 --> 01:54:55,959
...is to have no mercy...

1326
01:54:58,120 --> 01:54:59,919
..for the oppressor.

1327
01:55:28,760 --> 01:55:30,199
This dog died.

1328
01:55:32,000 --> 01:55:34,639
And you will get the hell out of my land.

1329
01:55:37,360 --> 01:55:40,199
If you ever show your faces...

1330
01:55:41,080 --> 01:55:42,279
...then...

1331
01:55:45,280 --> 01:55:47,759
...I will come
for you with my sword.

1332
01:56:10,640 --> 01:56:11,599
Oh Allah.

1333
01:56:13,280 --> 01:56:16,439
Help me to stand against the oppressors.

1334
01:56:18,640 --> 01:56:21,599
Give me the strength to fight for the weak.

1335
01:56:24,280 --> 01:56:25,319
Ameen.

1336
01:56:42,320 --> 01:56:44,359
You did good.

1337
01:56:48,520 --> 01:56:51,319
We fulfilled our last duty my bey.

1338
01:56:59,680 --> 01:57:00,959
My bey.

1339
01:57:02,160 --> 01:57:04,879
Was it our last one?

1340
01:57:09,240 --> 01:57:11,639
Will you be able to forgive us?

1341
01:57:22,040 --> 01:57:24,399
People make mistakes.

1342
01:57:24,400 --> 01:57:25,999
You...

1343
01:57:26,680 --> 01:57:30,079
...payed for the price of your mistakes.

1344
01:57:32,440 --> 01:57:35,199
But while you were paying for it...

1345
01:57:35,600 --> 01:57:38,879
...you didn't stop helping our nation.

1346
01:57:39,040 --> 01:57:40,319
Thank you.

1347
01:57:43,440 --> 01:57:45,079
That's why...

1348
01:57:46,200 --> 01:57:48,759
...you deserve to be forgiven.

1349
01:57:51,920 --> 01:57:53,919
Thank you my bey.

1350
01:58:00,000 --> 01:58:02,959
May Allah give you a long life.

1351
01:58:09,440 --> 01:58:11,719
Thank you my bey.

1352
01:58:14,480 --> 01:58:16,439
What's important is...

1353
01:58:17,320 --> 01:58:19,879
What's important is the nation.

1354
01:58:20,480 --> 01:58:22,999
What's important is our rules.

1355
01:58:27,640 --> 01:58:29,079
Now.

1356
01:58:30,560 --> 01:58:33,799
We get our strength from you.

1357
01:58:34,880 --> 01:58:37,639
We trust you fully.

1358
01:58:38,040 --> 01:58:40,839
If you make a mistake...

1359
01:58:41,680 --> 01:58:44,439
...then the
nation makes a mistake.

1360
01:58:45,880 --> 01:58:47,399
This will be never...

1361
01:58:48,120 --> 01:58:50,519
...repeated.

1362
01:58:50,680 --> 01:58:54,679
Never, my bey.

1363
01:58:55,960 --> 01:58:56,639
Cerkutay.

1364
01:58:56,640 --> 01:58:57,079
My bey.

1365
01:58:57,080 --> 01:58:59,039
Give them their belongings.

1366
01:58:59,640 --> 01:59:01,839
As you wish my bey.

1367
01:59:12,200 --> 01:59:16,679
I've taken care of these swords like my own.

1368
01:59:19,040 --> 01:59:22,679
Finally they're reunited with their owners.

1369
01:59:23,200 --> 01:59:25,599
Thanks brother.

1370
01:59:40,800 --> 01:59:44,799
Gunduz Bey who we got strength from until now...

1371
01:59:46,160 --> 01:59:49,919
Now we're going to fulfill our last duty for him.

1372
01:59:59,920 --> 02:00:01,479
Dad...

1373
02:00:04,560 --> 02:00:08,519
My dad whose heart was set
ablaze with the love for ghaza.

1374
02:00:13,080 --> 02:00:16,399
We took the life of the one who did this to you.

1375
02:00:17,640 --> 02:00:21,239
We're going to find who is behind this too.

1376
02:00:21,640 --> 02:00:23,759
I promise, dad.

1377
02:00:27,880 --> 02:00:30,519
Now you're a martyr.

1378
02:00:30,760 --> 02:00:33,079
And I'm an orphan.

1379
02:00:33,920 --> 02:00:36,919
But don't worry dad.

1380
02:00:37,160 --> 02:00:38,679
Your tribe..

1381
02:00:38,680 --> 02:00:41,279
...and your people will be under my care.

1382
02:00:41,280 --> 02:00:44,079
Even if I'm left all alone...

1383
02:00:44,360 --> 02:00:47,839
...I will protect them with my life dad.

1384
02:00:48,480 --> 02:00:50,319
I swear.

1385
02:00:50,320 --> 02:00:53,199
What are you saying Elcim?

1386
02:00:53,760 --> 02:00:55,919
You're not alone.

1387
02:00:55,920 --> 02:00:58,999
Not at all.

1388
02:01:00,520 --> 02:01:03,919
We're a family now.

1389
02:01:06,000 --> 02:01:08,159
From now on..

1390
02:01:08,400 --> 02:01:11,039
...I'll always be with you.

1391
02:01:12,080 --> 02:01:14,639
Don't look at me like that.

1392
02:01:15,600 --> 02:01:19,119
I know what those eyes are telling me.

1393
02:01:20,960 --> 02:01:23,359
But I promise you.

1394
02:01:24,320 --> 02:01:26,119
I promise...

1395
02:01:26,280 --> 02:01:29,119
...I'll always be there for you.

1396
02:01:30,200 --> 02:01:32,239
Gunduz Bey...

1397
02:01:35,320 --> 02:01:38,239
...trusted me with you.

1398
02:01:42,920 --> 02:01:45,879
I'll never leave you alone.

1399
02:01:55,320 --> 02:01:58,719
My dad is coming here to bury Gunduz Bey.

1400
02:01:58,840 --> 02:02:00,719
We should cover him.

1401
02:02:02,440 --> 02:02:04,999
In the name
of Allah, the merciful, the beneficent.

1402
02:02:06,320 --> 02:02:08,159
Go ahead.

1403
02:02:59,200 --> 02:03:01,719
Yakup Bey.

1404
02:03:08,360 --> 02:03:11,919
Before I leave, I will tell you...

1405
02:03:12,240 --> 02:03:15,399
...about the truth.

1406
02:03:20,480 --> 02:03:23,519
I did not know you were in the caravan.

1407
02:03:26,800 --> 02:03:29,559
Believe it if you want.

1408
02:03:30,440 --> 02:03:32,919
Or don't.

1409
02:03:37,360 --> 02:03:39,519
I believe it.

1410
02:03:44,160 --> 02:03:45,719
Are you...

1411
02:03:46,600 --> 02:03:49,039
...going there to-

1412
02:03:52,560 --> 02:03:54,559
No.

1413
02:03:57,480 --> 02:04:00,519
I stand behind what I said.

1414
02:04:04,520 --> 02:04:04,919
I told you the truth...

1415
02:04:04,920 --> 02:04:07,679
I told you the truth..

1416
02:04:08,600 --> 02:04:11,439
...so that you
wouldn't confuse me with yourselves.

1417
02:04:13,520 --> 02:04:15,639
Come on Mehmet.

1418
02:04:16,320 --> 02:04:21,839
One day, you will regret choosing
this life, and ignoring your family.

1419
02:04:25,800 --> 02:04:30,559
Mehmet, she is deaf to the truth.

1420
02:04:34,240 --> 02:04:36,239
It's futile talking to her.

1421
02:04:42,080 --> 02:04:43,759
Come on.

1422
02:04:43,840 --> 02:04:45,359
Enough!

1423
02:04:45,760 --> 02:04:47,999
Enough Yakup Bey!

1424
02:04:48,400 --> 02:04:51,119
You are the one who is deaf to the truth!

1425
02:04:52,440 --> 02:04:55,199
You are the one who can't see the truth!

1426
02:05:02,600 --> 02:05:07,039
I will not allow you to make my
hatun sad with your stone hearts!

1427
02:05:07,040 --> 02:05:09,719
Shut up Alaeddin

1428
02:05:11,440 --> 02:05:14,039
Or I am going to kill you

1429
02:05:16,880 --> 02:05:19,799
You ruined our family!

1430
02:05:22,520 --> 02:05:25,359
If you loved Gonca..

1431
02:05:25,520 --> 02:05:28,639
...you wouldn't punish her with this loneliness.

1432
02:05:30,280 --> 02:05:31,799
Mehmet.

1433
02:05:32,240 --> 02:05:35,399
Gonca is not alone, Mehmet Bey!

1434
02:05:43,360 --> 02:05:46,439
Gonca has her husband behind her.

1435
02:05:47,520 --> 02:05:49,879
And behind him, we stand.

1436
02:05:50,240 --> 02:05:52,519
Kayi tribe

1437
02:05:57,080 --> 02:06:00,439
You can't scare us with loneliness!

1438
02:06:03,680 --> 02:06:06,439
Safe travels to you.

1439
02:06:07,200 --> 02:06:09,759
Come on Mehmet!

1440
02:07:12,920 --> 02:07:16,439
...has delivered his soul to Allah today.

1441
02:07:21,400 --> 02:07:22,599
We know...

1442
02:07:23,120 --> 02:07:26,079
...that death and life...

1443
02:07:26,080 --> 02:07:28,079
...are under Allah's command.

1444
02:07:29,440 --> 02:07:32,039
May Allah lead us to the way of victory.

1445
02:07:33,120 --> 02:07:35,399
We faced many horrid traps.

1446
02:07:36,440 --> 02:07:40,239
Our hearts were pierced by evil arrows.

1447
02:07:41,120 --> 02:07:43,159
But our fallen soldiers are martyrs...

1448
02:07:43,960 --> 02:07:45,959
...and our survivors are ghazi.

1449
02:07:46,160 --> 02:07:48,319
Thank Allah.

1450
02:07:52,360 --> 02:07:54,359
Hang on Elcim Hatun.

1451
02:07:56,640 --> 02:07:57,879
Hang on.

1452
02:08:05,000 --> 02:08:08,079
Today, for the Ultimate Order...

1453
02:08:08,520 --> 02:08:10,079
...we had another martyr.

1454
02:08:10,680 --> 02:08:13,879
But we'll have a thousand more.

1455
02:08:16,840 --> 02:08:18,639
The pain we feel for Gunduz Bey...

1456
02:08:19,000 --> 02:08:21,039
...won't be seen by the enemy.

1457
02:08:23,880 --> 02:08:25,039
Like Gunduz Bey...

1458
02:08:25,720 --> 02:08:29,479
...many brave soldiers have passed.

1459
02:08:30,520 --> 02:08:32,519
But we will avenge them.

1460
02:08:32,520 --> 02:08:34,519
We will!

1461
02:08:42,320 --> 02:08:43,799
My son.

1462
02:08:44,720 --> 02:08:46,519
Ahmet.

1463
02:08:50,520 --> 02:08:51,879
My son.

1464
02:08:54,320 --> 02:08:58,159
How can I leave my heart here and leave?

1465
02:08:59,840 --> 02:09:01,399
How can I leave?

1466
02:09:01,560 --> 02:09:02,719
Shut up!

1467
02:09:03,120 --> 02:09:04,399
Melike Hatun.

1468
02:09:21,560 --> 02:09:23,119
I will punish you...

1469
02:09:24,320 --> 02:09:26,319
...when we get to Sinop.

1470
02:09:30,520 --> 02:09:31,879
Shut up now.

1471
02:09:36,200 --> 02:09:37,559
My son..

1472
02:09:39,200 --> 02:09:40,199
I'll go now.

1473
02:09:42,760 --> 02:09:45,159
But not because I give up.

1474
02:09:45,920 --> 02:09:48,199
I'll come back stronger.

1475
02:09:54,720 --> 02:09:56,959
These lands you rest in...

1476
02:09:58,520 --> 02:10:00,759
...I won't let Osman have them.

1477
02:10:02,360 --> 02:10:05,439
I'll take all of the lands he has.

1478
02:10:06,640 --> 02:10:07,239
And...

1479
02:10:09,240 --> 02:10:10,839
..I'll be back...

1480
02:10:11,840 --> 02:10:14,239
...to punish him and his family.

1481
02:10:26,000 --> 02:10:27,599
Come on Melike Hatun.

1482
02:10:53,680 --> 02:10:56,199
I won't follow you anymore Ibrahim Bey.

1483
02:11:00,320 --> 02:11:02,039
Where are you going Tugay?

1484
02:11:02,040 --> 02:11:04,239
You don't follow Allah's path.

1485
02:11:06,600 --> 02:11:09,279
I'll go where I belong now.

1486
02:11:23,920 --> 02:11:25,119
Come on Hatun.

1487
02:11:49,640 --> 02:11:50,839
I swear...

1488
02:11:52,080 --> 02:11:54,199
...I won't let Gonca stay there.

1489
02:11:55,400 --> 02:11:57,359
I'll kill Alaeddin if I have to.

1490
02:11:58,280 --> 02:12:00,399
But I won't let Gonca stay there.

1491
02:12:06,000 --> 02:12:08,239
He took my daughter.

1492
02:12:09,760 --> 02:12:12,319
He took my market.

1493
02:12:13,840 --> 02:12:17,359
He took my daughter's trust in me.

1494
02:12:21,920 --> 02:12:25,599
You're going to pay for these Osman.

1495
02:12:26,440 --> 02:12:29,759
You're going to pay for these.

1496
02:12:46,680 --> 02:12:49,519
What will I tell to Sadet?

1497
02:12:51,000 --> 02:12:52,559
How can I..

1498
02:12:55,600 --> 02:12:58,599
...leave my daughter here?

1499
02:13:05,080 --> 02:13:07,839
Dad.

1500
02:13:08,720 --> 02:13:10,559
I'm okay.

1501
02:13:13,160 --> 02:13:14,719
I'm okay.

1502
02:13:24,280 --> 02:13:26,919
I'm leaving my heart here.

1503
02:13:59,000 --> 02:14:01,599
But I'll be back.

1504
02:14:07,360 --> 02:14:11,279
I'll come back stronger than before.

1505
02:14:12,560 --> 02:14:15,079
We will be back Mehmet.

1506
02:14:18,160 --> 02:14:20,119
We will be back.

1507
02:14:43,720 --> 02:14:45,079
Now...

1508
02:14:45,280 --> 02:14:48,399
...we're going
to send Gunduz Bey to his resting place.

1509
02:14:48,400 --> 02:14:50,239
Don't forget this.

1510
02:14:50,240 --> 02:14:52,399
The blood we shed..

1511
02:14:52,400 --> 02:14:55,399
...is never for nothing.

1512
02:14:58,000 --> 02:15:00,879
The blood of our martyrs...

1513
02:15:01,200 --> 02:15:03,439
...is the messenger of a great nation...

1514
02:15:03,840 --> 02:15:06,279
...and the seed of a great nation.

1515
02:15:06,280 --> 02:15:09,479
If Allah permits!

1516
02:15:15,440 --> 02:15:17,239
Come on.

1517
02:15:18,400 --> 02:15:20,799
May Allah forgive his sins.

1518
02:15:21,520 --> 02:15:23,799
In the name
of Allah, the merciful, the beneficent.

1519
02:15:31,720 --> 02:15:34,079
Oh Allah, in the name of Allah,
the merciful, the beneficent.

1520
02:15:34,160 --> 02:15:39,799
Allah is the Greatest!

1521
02:15:39,800 --> 02:15:44,919
There is none worthy of worship except Allah.

1522
02:15:44,920 --> 02:15:50,359
Allah is the Greatest!

1523
02:15:50,360 --> 02:15:56,359
There is none worthy of worship except Allah.

1524
02:15:56,360 --> 02:16:00,719
Allah is the Greatest!

1525
02:16:00,720 --> 02:16:05,319
There is none worthy of worship except Allah.

1526
02:16:05,320 --> 02:16:10,959
Allah is the Greatest!

1527
02:16:10,960 --> 02:16:15,879
There is none worthy of worship except Allah.

1528
02:16:16,000 --> 02:16:19,959
Conquer Bursa, Osman Bey.

1529
02:16:23,640 --> 02:16:28,159
I will conquer Bursa and every other city!

1530
02:16:29,240 --> 02:16:33,599
I will bring justice to this corrupt system!

1531
